{"season":"2004-05","source":"espn","maxWeek":24,"rankings":{"ind":[{"week":1,"rank":1,"record":"3-0","summary":"Injuries? Pacers (Jermaine specifically) apparently don't even know that they're banged up. And Artest? Looking great after a summer of innuendo and trade rumors."},{"week":2,"rank":4,"record":"5-2","summary":"As soon as someone (us) writes a Power Rankings comment about how Artest is 'looking great,' chaos ensues. Pacers never should issued him (Rodman's) No. 91."},{"week":3,"rank":10,"record":"7-3","summary":"You can make the case that Pacers, in their depleted state, should be dropped into the 20s. I just didn't have the heart to do that to suffering Pacer People. Yet."},{"week":4,"rank":8,"record":"10-4","summary":"The committee questioned Indy's depth last season, calling it mythical. No one can dare say so this season if Pacers keep winning without their three best players."},{"week":5,"rank":15,"record":"10-7","summary":"No one in the locker room is counting the shopping days 'til Christmas. The only countdown of consequence in Indy: 40 days 'til Jermaine returns, unless the appeal shortens the wait."},{"week":6,"rank":21,"record":"10-10","summary":"It's official. After seven straight post-brawl defeats, you can pretty safely say they're missing Jermaine, SJax and Ronnie, as Larry Legend likes to call him."},{"week":7,"rank":20,"record":"12-11","summary":"The latest from a season in flux: NBA announces that All-Star votes for Artest won't count, and Carlisle's count is up to 15 different starting lineups already."},{"week":8,"rank":16,"record":"12-13","summary":"Pacers have slipped below .500 for the first time all season. But, again, only Miami has pulled away in the East -- and Indy will keep rising, naturally, if O'Neal stays unsuspended."},{"week":9,"rank":9,"record":"16-13","summary":"With O'Neal's suspension officially reduced and S-Jax coming back in just over three weeks, the committee has a feeling that Indy will be filling the troublesome No. 5 slot very soon."},{"week":10,"rank":13,"record":"16-16","summary":"Have you seen this portion of the schedule? Yet another reason for Pacer People to think the league is anti-Indy: Spurs, Mavs, Suns and Grizz on the road, then Suns at home."},{"week":11,"rank":14,"record":"18-17","summary":"Pacers are only 6-5 since the return of J. O'Neal. But it ain't his fault: JO is the league's leading scorer this month, at 33.9 ppg."},{"week":12,"rank":15,"record":"20-19","summary":"Pacers are a mere 13-17 since The Malice of Auburn Hills, but Stephen Jackson's return is quite timely, with Uncle Reggie only averaging 9.2 ppg in January (down from 17.7 in December)."},{"week":13,"rank":21,"record":"20-22","summary":"Since they went to Miami and won in OT, Pacers have dropped four straight -- and Tinsley, since scorching Heat for 30, is just 10 for 41 from the field, thanks to his flu bug."},{"week":14,"rank":21,"record":"22-24","summary":"At just 15-22 since The Malice of Auburn Hills, Indiana has seemingly done the impossible ... give the Atlantic Division hope of sending two teams to the playoffs."},{"week":15,"rank":19,"record":"24-26","summary":"This isn't why he retired, but just to show you how far below expectations Indy has fallen: Uncle Reg recently missed eight of 18 free throws -- and let Croshere shoot a technical."},{"week":16,"rank":19,"record":"25-26","summary":"Never, ever thought we'd have to trot out our trusty Indy .500 line this season. Yet that's where Pacers continue to hover."},{"week":17,"rank":16,"record":"28-27","summary":"It appears Pacers weren't pleased when Carlisle announced that ''we're not an elite team.'' They've responded with a 6-2 uptick, Indy's best run since a 6-2 start before the brawl."},{"week":18,"rank":19,"record":"29-30","summary":"You see Jermaine tweak his shoulder and you have to ask: Haven't these guys, or at least their fans, suffered enough?"},{"week":19,"rank":18,"record":"31-31","summary":"For the first time since 1972, the state has no team in the NCAA Tournament. And if Jermaine's shoulder doesn't heal soon, Pacers won't be cheering up anyone in the nation's heartland."},{"week":20,"rank":13,"record":"33-32","summary":"Carlisle won't win 50 games for the first time in four seasons, but he has to be a Coach of the Year factor if Pacers can make the playoffs after all they've been through."},{"week":21,"rank":14,"record":"35-34","summary":"How good a coaching job has Carlisle done? Consider that Pacers' projected starting lineup of Tinsley, Miller, Artest, Foster and O'Neal has combined to play zero games together."},{"week":22,"rank":10,"record":"38-34","summary":"The way these guys are rolling without J. O'Neal -- specifically Reggie, who averaged 19.1 ppg in 31.2 mpg in March -- Pacers have to be the East's most feared bracket buster."},{"week":23,"rank":12,"record":"41-35","summary":"This will be the first team in history (full seasons only) with fewer than 52 wins after a 60-win season, but we repeat: Carlisle has never coached better, keeping Indy over .500 on its roller coaster."},{"week":24,"rank":15,"record":"43-37","summary":"Losing to Miami in Jermaine's return, after Shaq got hurt, was a bit of a downer. Here's the pick-me-up: Pacers went on a season-saving run of 15-7 while their O'Neal was out injured."}],"uta":[{"week":1,"rank":2,"record":"3-0","summary":"In midseason form already, Jazz waste no time making us look foolish for even suggesting that the PG injuries (Arroyo and Lopez) would slow these guys down."},{"week":2,"rank":2,"record":"5-1","summary":"Committee deemed Jazz not quite ready for the No. 1 slot after its Toronto loss. But the response -- pounding on banged-up Detroit -- couldn't have been more emphatic."},{"week":3,"rank":4,"record":"7-3","summary":"Of greater concern than the losses in Fla. (big to Orlando, unlucky in Miami) is the defensive slippage. Giving up 100-plus points in three of last week's four games was not so Jazzy."},{"week":4,"rank":14,"record":"8-6","summary":"Jazz have obviously been reading too much fawning press (probably on ESPN.com). How on Earth could a Jerry Sloan team be the cure-all for New Orleans AND Chicago? And at home?"},{"week":5,"rank":17,"record":"8-9","summary":"Bad time to lose AK-47. The first four games without their defensive ace saw Jazz face Spurs, Suns, Sonics and Mavs ... with only Phoenix, the hottest road team, at the Delta Center."},{"week":6,"rank":23,"record":"9-12","summary":"How much will Jazz miss AK-47 for the next month? Well, let's see: Utah is 1-6 without him and allowing just under 107 ppg over the past eight games."},{"week":7,"rank":24,"record":"10-15","summary":"At 4-14 since a 6-1 start, it's probably safe to say Jazz aren't as deep as we thought. Losing one guy, even if it's AK-47, shouldn't hurt them this much. Should it?"},{"week":8,"rank":26,"record":"11-16","summary":"Time for Kirilenko to renegotiate. Clearly AK-47 is deserving of a new contract . . . he might be worth more than the max to Jazz, who've stunned us by falling this far."},{"week":9,"rank":27,"record":"11-20","summary":"As Utah's freefall continues, maybe we have to rewind to last season and give AK-47 more of the credit Sloan got for getting that Jazz to 42-40. This Jazz, still sans AK-47, just gets worse."},{"week":10,"rank":28,"record":"11-24","summary":"The wait for AK-47's return has grown so interminable that some dark thoughts -- about this slide eventually driving Sloan away -- have begun to torment the committee."},{"week":11,"rank":24,"record":"13-26","summary":"After their horrific slide sans AK-47, Jazz stunningly became the first team in history, this deep into the season, to win back-to-back against teams with winning percentages of .800 or better."},{"week":12,"rank":25,"record":"14-28","summary":"Some fun NBA trivia for your next party: Name the only teams to beat San Antonio and Phoenix this season. That's right: Sacramento, Memphis and somehow this (struggling) Jazz."},{"week":13,"rank":24,"record":"15-30","summary":"AK-47 is back, thankfully, but even he might not be able to prevent the worst first half in Jazz history. Utah had 37 losses at the break in 1979-80, its first season in Salt Lake City."},{"week":14,"rank":25,"record":"16-31","summary":"10-30 record since a 6-1 start makes for some hard-to-believe reading. And Kirilenko clearly isn't a cure-all just yet."},{"week":15,"rank":26,"record":"17-33","summary":"The owner ripping Boozer publicly grabbed the headlines, but the bigger topic on our minds is: If Stock retired last year ... and Karl retired this year ... is Sloan (gasp) next?"},{"week":16,"rank":27,"record":"17-35","summary":"Even if Miller wants to deal Boozer, our suspicion is that savvy GM O'Connor will talk him out of it. It's way too soon to give up on the first marquee free agent to ever choose Utah."},{"week":17,"rank":26,"record":"18-37","summary":"Of all the forgettable aspects in a nightmare season, put this up high: Utah is (gasp) 1-8 against Atlantic Division residents."},{"week":18,"rank":26,"record":"20-39","summary":"What so many of us expected to happen last season is unavoidably happening now: Jerry Sloan is just three losses away from his first sub-.500 season in Utah."},{"week":19,"rank":27,"record":"20-42","summary":"Fresh off what might be his best job ever -- 42-40 in his first season without Mailman and Stock -- Sloan is officially a losing coach for the first time since taking over Jazz in 1988."},{"week":20,"rank":27,"record":"20-46","summary":"The depths of Utah's struggles are simply hard to believe. Jerry Sloan has been stuck on 937 victories, one shy of tying Red Auerbach, since the first Jazz game of the month on March 2."},{"week":21,"rank":28,"record":"22-47","summary":"Raja Bell reluctantly conceded that Jazz have 'cashed it in.' Which tells you all you need to know about L.A.'s playoff chances when Lakers go to Utah and give up 115 points."},{"week":22,"rank":28,"record":"22-50","summary":"In this What Next season, now it's Boozer out for the season. Kirilenko was first, meaning that Utah's projected frontcourt stalwarts played just 25 games together in Year 1."},{"week":23,"rank":26,"record":"24-52","summary":"Utah's season peaked Nov. 13. Jazz and Sonics were tied atop the Northwest Division at 5-1 that day. But Seattle then won 14 of 18, Utah lost 15 of its next 21 and, well, now look."},{"week":24,"rank":27,"record":"25-55","summary":"Injuries were obviously a killer, but last season's  42-40 magic disappeared just before Thanksgiving ... when Jazz lost back-to-back home games to then-winless Hornets and Bulls."}],"mia":[{"week":1,"rank":3,"record":"3-0","summary":"An FYI, from Shaq: Dwyane Wade is now known as Flash. It really was Dwyane's World in Week 1, true, but Shaq's still in charge of passing out nicknames."},{"week":2,"rank":5,"record":"5-2","summary":"Like him or not, Shaq is a free-agent magnet. Shandon Anderson choose Miami over a clutch of teams and Zo wants to return to South Beach if Jersey buys him out. Et tu, Kobe?"},{"week":3,"rank":3,"record":"8-3","summary":"While folks continue to question their depth, Heat are soothing themselves by pounding East foes (7-0). And Pacers' woes mean that the path to the conference finals just got even easier."},{"week":4,"rank":5,"record":"10-5","summary":"Shaq's latest Flash praise/Kobe slam: '(Wade) is the best second-year player I've seen since Michael Jordan. He keeps everybody involved, and that's the sign of a great player.'"},{"week":5,"rank":9,"record":"11-7","summary":"Heat is now 10-2 against the East and 1-5 vs. the West. Miami's also hoping Shaq's hamstring is the real culprit for this trend: O'Neal has been held below 20 points in 8 of 18 games."},{"week":6,"rank":6,"record":"15-7","summary":"Opportunity is there, with Indiana in tatters and Detroit looking indifferent, for Heat to secure homecourt advantage throughout the East playoffs. Let's see if they capitalize."},{"week":7,"rank":4,"record":"19-7","summary":"Not to say they're three-dimensional or anything, but Heat are 9-0 against Washington, Milwaukee and Utah ... and just 10-7 against the rest of the league."},{"week":8,"rank":4,"record":"22-7","summary":"Heat should be feeling good about themselves. Miami's up to 6-5 vs. the West and, on top of Wade and Shaq, has two undrafted starters (D-Jones and Haslem) chipping in nicely."},{"week":9,"rank":1,"record":"25-7","summary":"Heat will love hearing this: The NBA's last four teams to go 14-1 in December all reached the Finals, and three of those four won it all (2000 Lakers, '81 Celtics and '72 Lakers)."},{"week":10,"rank":4,"record":"27-9","summary":"What a difference one Monday makes. Actually, the difference this Monday with Miami is two losses to Seattle, after 14 wins in a row, and a 7-7 record against the West."},{"week":11,"rank":4,"record":"28-11","summary":"Considering what circus-enforced road trips have done to Bulls -- who are 1-38 on such trips since MJ quit -- Heat can handle going 2-3 out West while Ringling Bros. invaded Miami."},{"week":12,"rank":6,"record":"30-12","summary":"No question Heat's record against the West could be better (9-9), but perhaps we should be more impressed with that 21-3 record within the East. Just throwing it out there."},{"week":13,"rank":5,"record":"33-13","summary":"Jim Jackson was on Miami's wish list and Zo still might be. Had they acquired both, Heat would have boasted the top four picks from the '92 draft, along with Shaq and Laettner."},{"week":14,"rank":4,"record":"35-14","summary":"Shaq can make all the jokes he wants about Don Nelson being ''the Jack Haley of his era,'' but the irony is this: Heat can only wish they had a sixth man as reliable as Nellie was."},{"week":15,"rank":3,"record":"39-14","summary":"Heat take a lot of, well, heat for their record against the West, but Sunday's win over SA makes them a passable 12-10. Better than 1978's Bullets, who won it all as a sub-.500 team vs. West."},{"week":16,"rank":4,"record":"40-14","summary":"Zo's arrival will give Miami the top three picks from the '92 draft, joining Shaq and Laettner. Weirder still: Miami has had eight of the top 10 players from that draft, plus No. 12 Harold Miner."},{"week":17,"rank":6,"record":"42-16","summary":"The way Detroit's playing, you get the feeling Heat need to sign Zo and GP to win the East ... and get Shaq well, obviously."},{"week":18,"rank":4,"record":"45-16","summary":"Heat is due an apology. After last week, Miami's oft-trashed record vs. the West (14-10) is no worse than Detroit's (13-10)."},{"week":19,"rank":2,"record":"48-16","summary":"How hot are Heat? Try this hot: Miami hasn't lost a game in regulation since Feb. 1. Heat's only two losses in the past 17 games came in overtime -- and both without Shaq."},{"week":20,"rank":1,"record":"52-16","summary":"First team to win 50 games this season. First team to clinch a playoff berth this season. First team to post two 10-game win streaks this season. In short, no one's hotter."},{"week":21,"rank":2,"record":"53-18","summary":"Sorry. Don't care how impressive Heat looked winning at Suns' pace. Lose to Charlotte the next night and you forfeit No. 1."},{"week":22,"rank":2,"record":"55-19","summary":"In case you still need convincing that Shaq makes a difference, be advised that Heat had only 13 road wins last season ... compared to 22 already with five road games left."},{"week":23,"rank":5,"record":"56-21","summary":"Heat would never be this low if Shaq were playing. More than one cynic, mind you, has wondered aloud about whether Shaq is really ill or simply saving some fuel for the playoffs."},{"week":24,"rank":6,"record":"57-23","summary":"S. Van Gundy is undoubtedly panicky about the way his Heat are stumbling to the finish line, but at least one recent trend is encouraging: Zo has averaged 23.2 mpg since April 8."}],"det":[{"week":1,"rank":4,"record":"2-1","summary":"Took Toronto lightly (bad) and didn't even deny it (worse). Hence the drop of three slots, and a stern warning, because complacency might be Pistons' biggest enemy this season."},{"week":2,"rank":7,"record":"3-3","summary":"Take away Ben Wallace, Chauncey Billups and Larry Brown and look what happens. Pistons are averaging 96.0 points per game -- and allowing (gasp) 98.7."},{"week":3,"rank":9,"record":"5-4","summary":"You could argue that Pistons deserve a bigger drop for their role (and their fans' role) in The Malice of Auburn Hills. You can bet that the commitee will take action if the league doesn't."},{"week":4,"rank":10,"record":"6-7","summary":"Pistons are struggling so much without the suspended Big Ben that the committee is starting to think it overestimated the revamped champs' depth."},{"week":5,"rank":6,"record":"8-8","summary":"Getting better with Ben back, but they had to get better. Pistons were .500 only once last season -- this season we've seen the champs mired at 1-1, 3-3, 4-4, 5-5, 6-6, 7-7 and 8-8."},{"week":6,"rank":8,"record":"10-10","summary":"Being the only team this month to shackle the NBA's top scorer (Nowitzki) obviously didn't cure Detroit of its post-championship blahs. Pistons aren't close to playing Larry's 'right way.'"},{"week":7,"rank":7,"record":"12-11","summary":"How the mighty have fallen. According to the Elias Sports Bureau, Pistons rank 30th in bench points per game (16.6). Phoenix is No. 29 at 18.4, but Suns aren't known for their bench."},{"week":8,"rank":7,"record":"13-12","summary":"It's only scant consolation, but at least it's something: Pistons are the only team in the East, and one of only three in the whole league, holding opponents under 90 ppg."},{"week":9,"rank":6,"record":"16-13","summary":"Pistons will hate hearing this: NBA has only seen two defending champs with worse records entering the New Year than Detroit at 15-13. That's '03 Lakers (13-19) and '77 Celtics (17-15)."},{"week":10,"rank":6,"record":"18-14","summary":"Pistons are still looking for pick-me-ups, and here's one -- Detroit was 16-13 entering the new year in 1990 . . . and went on to win the title. So don't give up on them just yet."},{"week":11,"rank":5,"record":"22-14","summary":"Pistons are finally starting to roll, but here's the new concern: Detroit's starters are playing as much as the Phoenix starters. Which can't be good for their playoff preparations."},{"week":12,"rank":10,"record":"23-17","summary":"After winning six in a row to suggest they're finally back, Pistons drop three in a row for the first time all season. Which pretty much muted any Arroyo trade celebrations."},{"week":13,"rank":8,"record":"26-18","summary":"Knicks might be his dream job, but here's Larry Brown's reality: His current players can't help but be ticked to be incessantly nitpicked -- and then hear Lar gush about NYC mystique."},{"week":14,"rank":9,"record":"28-19","summary":"Whine all you want to, Detroiters, but you have some nerve complaining to us about our All-Star picks given the rankings respect the champs always get here, at just a half-game ahead of Wiz."},{"week":15,"rank":7,"record":"30-19","summary":"Looks like they're getting serious again, and maybe this time they'll stay serious ... and stay on this sudden 50-win pace."},{"week":16,"rank":6,"record":"32-19","summary":"This time, it really looks like they're back. Pistons survived the toughest part of their schedule (seven back-to-backs in January) and rank as one of only two teams holding teams under 90 ppg."},{"week":17,"rank":1,"record":"35-19","summary":"It took a lot longer than we expected for the defending champs to get back up here, but Pistons are 20-6 since Jan. 1. Which suddenly makes them the league's hottest team."},{"week":18,"rank":5,"record":"36-22","summary":"On the verge of a win in Phoenix, Pistons collapsed and still haven't recovered. Which, not surprisingly, has prompted a wave of mindless You Jinxed Us e-mails out of Michigan."},{"week":19,"rank":5,"record":"38-23","summary":"Pistons can't catch Miami, and chances are no one can catch Pistons and bump them out of the No. 2 spot. So it's as good a time as there is for Larry to take time off to get healthy."},{"week":20,"rank":2,"record":"42-23","summary":"Prince looks more like a Most Improved Player favorite every day ... and Gar Heard's fortunes as interim coach (3-0 in this fill-in stint compared to 2-4 last time) are improving, too."},{"week":21,"rank":6,"record":"43-26","summary":"Why is a Lakers comparison so apt for these switch-flippers? One Detroit observer we trust says the champs' problem is arrogance against lesser teams. Just like the old Lakers."},{"week":22,"rank":7,"record":"46-27","summary":"Pistons players can get frustrated with Larry, but they do miss him at times, too. To wit, they're 9-8 without him and followed up a 9-1 record February with a 9-8 March."},{"week":23,"rank":6,"record":"49-27","summary":"Instead of saying this is the win streak that proves Detroit Is Back, let's assume the champs have been so up-and-down because they've known for a while that Miami was uncatchable."},{"week":24,"rank":5,"record":"53-27","summary":"What's the highest compliment we can give the champs? They placed no one on the committee's All-NBA team, but even without a top-15 player they remain our pick to win the East."}],"sas":[{"week":1,"rank":5,"record":"2-1","summary":"Another team, like Detroit, that should never slip below Utah. But, like Detroit, Spurs took a road game lightly (Seattle) and got embarrassed."},{"week":2,"rank":3,"record":"5-1","summary":"Spurs can't go higher after two gimme wins (Warriors, Hawks) . . . and with Parker pressing to impress (.346 from the field) . . . and with Duncan's ongoing FT woes (.591)."},{"week":3,"rank":1,"record":"8-2","summary":"Would have been an easy call had Spurs finished off Toronto properly. They're winning, yeah, but you can be sure Pop doesn't want to reward them after Sunday's fourth-quarter disaster."},{"week":4,"rank":2,"record":"11-3","summary":"Committee, as you know, doesn't believe in jinxes. But those who do no doubt noticed that Spurs, like Mavs the week before, lost their first game after claiming the No. 1 ranking."},{"week":5,"rank":1,"record":"15-3","summary":"Perhaps the best part about Spurs' start is all the rest Duncan's getting. TD is averaging just 34.9 mpg because SA has been so dominant, and that's mileage saved for the playoffs."},{"week":6,"rank":3,"record":"17-5","summary":"Far, far worse than surrendering T-Mac's 13 points in 35 seconds was falling behind, 60-41, at halftime to Seattle. It was the biggest halftime home deficit in Duncan's career."},{"week":7,"rank":2,"record":"20-5","summary":"Not that anyone's terribly concerned in the Alamo City, but it is interesting: Duncan has failed to score 20 points in two straight games. First time all season that's happened."},{"week":8,"rank":3,"record":"22-6","summary":"Committee feels safe in saying that Spurs will win most nights if they keep scoring 96 a game. Another surprise: San Antonio is 7-2 on the second night of back-to-backs somehow."},{"week":9,"rank":2,"record":"25-7","summary":"Torching Suns should have been good enough for the top spot. But then Spurs lost in Sacto . . . and Heat is too hot to ignore."},{"week":10,"rank":2,"record":"28-7","summary":"Duncan has failed to score 20 points in eight of 11 games . . . and Spurs couldn't care less. They're getting offense elsewhere and continue to save TD's gas for the playoffs."},{"week":11,"rank":1,"record":"30-9","summary":"The upsetting development, for Spurs fans, is not the 2-2 week. It's that now people will say SA is getting interesting ... just because Parker is dating a Desperate Housewife."},{"week":12,"rank":1,"record":"34-9","summary":"As stated Friday, the NBA's elite starts and ends with Spurs right now. They clearly deserve a second All-Star, but here's where we're not so sure: Is it Parker or the 48-point Manu?"},{"week":13,"rank":1,"record":"36-10","summary":"Comforting thought as Spurs hit the road: Entering the weekend, the teams left on their home schedule have the league's lowest combined winning percentage at .433."},{"week":14,"rank":1,"record":"38-10","summary":"This will be Pop's first All-Star game, but this is far more important: Pop and Larry Brown are the only active coaches with a championship ring now that Rudy T. has resigned."},{"week":15,"rank":4,"record":"40-12","summary":"A rejection from Mailman won't stop Spurs' search for another big man. Especially after a loss to Miami, days before Heat even have a chance to tag team Zo with Shaq."},{"week":16,"rank":1,"record":"41-12","summary":"Apparently all the teams around San Antonio didn't like seeing Spurs punished with a steep drop, either. So they helped SA get back where it belongs to start the stretch run."},{"week":17,"rank":2,"record":"42-13","summary":"Nabbing Nazr was a steal, but hold off on saying it might have been the best move on deadline day. The same tag, remember, was slapped on the summer signing of Brent Barry."},{"week":18,"rank":2,"record":"46-13","summary":"Make that two Duncan injury scares this season. Enough to make everyone in San Antonio skittish, in other words."},{"week":19,"rank":3,"record":"47-15","summary":"Common sense says they'll be back at No. 1 before long and enter the playoffs as the title favorite. But for now, until Duncan and Ginobili are healthy, Spurs can't go higher than this."},{"week":20,"rank":4,"record":"50-16","summary":"For the seventh straight full season, Spurs have won 50 games. But this group is only 1-3 without Duncan, so expect a longer rest after this ankle twist to ensure TD's playoff health."},{"week":21,"rank":3,"record":"52-18","summary":"Pop thinks Duncan will make an appearance during the final five games of the regular season. Dare we say, even without TD until the playoffs, Spurs will hang on to a top-two seed."},{"week":22,"rank":3,"record":"54-19","summary":"Spurs are nearly back to .500 without Duncan (5-6), and dare we also say Duncan can find a playoff rhythm quickly even if he doesn't play before the regular season ends."},{"week":23,"rank":3,"record":"57-20","summary":"Winning those back-to-back games in double OT -- the second without Manu and Duncan -- halted a 1-6 road skid and eased fears that Spurs could wind up blowing the Southwest lead."},{"week":24,"rank":3,"record":"59-21","summary":"It didn't always seem so with Duncan missing 16 games (9-7), but this actually was a fairly easy season for the most versatile Spurs yet. Forty of S.A.'s 59 wins are by 10 points or more."}],"min":[{"week":1,"rank":6,"record":"2-1","summary":"This much we know already: KG looks as serious as ever, and Wolves vs. Nuggets in a playoff rematch (fingers crossed) would be serious fun."},{"week":2,"rank":6,"record":"3-2","summary":"There's not much more KG can do out there, but Sam I Am's struggles offensively and defensively suggest Cassell's hip could still be a problem. Which would be a huge problem."},{"week":3,"rank":5,"record":"5-3","summary":"Wolves have been a bit quiet, but that should change this week. They've got five games between now and Sunday -- at Mavs, Pacers and Kings, home to Supes and Grizz."},{"week":4,"rank":4,"record":"8-5","summary":"The best thing you can say about Wolves' up-and-down start is that they were 9-8 in November last season. And you surely remember how that turned out."},{"week":5,"rank":2,"record":"11-5","summary":"Sam I Am is finally heating up and KG was already scorching. How scorching? Six times already KG has been two assists or less away from a triple-double."},{"week":6,"rank":4,"record":"13-7","summary":"Obviously Wolves had no idea how much hate e-mail flooded in from the Pacific Northwest (i.e. Seattle fans) after last week's rankings. Surely they'd have lived up to billing had they known."},{"week":7,"rank":5,"record":"15-8","summary":"Nice little warmup for the X-Mas Day sked: KG vs. Duncan on Thursday in San Antonio. Wolves, though, have more losses this month already (7-3) than all of last December (11-2)."},{"week":8,"rank":6,"record":"16-10","summary":"Could this team be too deep? At just 8-5 in December, and with four straight road defeats, Flip has to be wondering."},{"week":9,"rank":8,"record":"16-12","summary":"It's not quite as bad as Kevin McHale claims -- ''We're probably the most underachieving team in the league,'' he says -- but Wolves' struggles haven't helped our search for a worthy No. 5."},{"week":10,"rank":11,"record":"17-15","summary":"The notion that Flip is in trouble? Laughable. But the 4-8 slump and teamwide indifference (KG and Wally aside)? No joke."},{"week":11,"rank":11,"record":"19-17","summary":"Wolves are the last team you'll see knee-jerk the coach out of his seat. If they can handle seven straight first-round exits, KG-McHale-Flip can get through a regular-season blip."},{"week":12,"rank":11,"record":"21-19","summary":"Wolves apparently want that eighth seed and a first-round matchup with San Antonio. If that possibility doesn't wake them up and snap them into focus, who knows what will?"},{"week":13,"rank":9,"record":"24-20","summary":"Now that they've got the lineup straightened out, with Wally going to the bench so Hassell can start, perhaps Wolves can fix this 7-11 record vs. the East . . . after a 24-6 mark last season."},{"week":14,"rank":20,"record":"24-24","summary":"All Wolves need now is a 34-0 finish to match last season's record. Anyone out there like their chances?"},{"week":15,"rank":20,"record":"25-27","summary":"No truth to the rumor that, to replace Flip, Wolves considered hiring the guy with the rolled-up magazine who squats across from their bench pretending to coach every home game."},{"week":16,"rank":15,"record":"27-27","summary":"At stake for Wolves is the league's second-longest active playoff streak. Minnesota has made eight straight trips to the post-season, second only to the Lakers' 10 in a row."},{"week":17,"rank":20,"record":"28-29","summary":"No one needed to make a trade more than Wolves, who couldn't unload Spree. The only consolation for Minny is that Lakers and Nuggets have tougher remaining schedules."},{"week":18,"rank":18,"record":"30-30","summary":"Oops. Upon reflection, Denver's spring schedule is actually easier than Minny's. Wolves play 12 of their last 22 on the road."},{"week":19,"rank":19,"record":"32-32","summary":"This might just be us jumping the gun, but it sure looks (to us) like Wolves just want the season to be over with."},{"week":20,"rank":14,"record":"34-34","summary":"Under Flip, Wolves were a game under .500. Under McHale, they're 9-8 and (uh-oh) four behind Denver in the loss column."},{"week":21,"rank":15,"record":"37-34","summary":"The good news? Wolves apparently haven't quit. The bad news? They probably waited too long to find a groove."},{"week":22,"rank":12,"record":"39-35","summary":"Did you see KG on TV after the win at Sac? His enthusiastic warning about Wolves ''coming'' strikes us as a good sign; it was the most KG-esque bravado we've seen from him for ages."},{"week":23,"rank":19,"record":"40-37","summary":"It's probably time for the committee (of one) to stop going on TV and saying Minny still has a shot at the No. 8 spot. KG's Wolves, in reality, aren't any more alive than Kobe's Lakers."},{"week":24,"rank":19,"record":"42-38","summary":"Here's a hunch that the best record of any non-playoff team isn't much consolation. Another hunch: McHale resigns as coach and GM, leaving Wolves to fill both posts before anything else."}],"dal":[{"week":1,"rank":7,"record":"3-0","summary":"Mavs have surprised even themselves with so much early continuity. And with their depth, you can be sure that Dallas will keep winning if it keeps holding teams to 92.3 ppg. A lot."},{"week":2,"rank":1,"record":"7-1","summary":"We say so again: If Mavs keep holding teams under 95 ppg and stay in the league's top two in FG defense (.400 even), they're not going to lose often."},{"week":3,"rank":8,"record":"8-3","summary":"Bad week for Dallas, and not because of the losses to Phoenix (home) and Denver (away). It's because of the losses: Dampier, Terry and now Nowitzki."},{"week":4,"rank":7,"record":"10-5","summary":"The good thing about knowing the pain of many ankle sprains, as Dirk would tell you, is knowing how to come back from them faster than the docs expect."},{"week":5,"rank":7,"record":"12-6","summary":"Common sense says Armstrong has to help Mavs' shaky passing game at least a little. Or maybe Nowitzki, arguably Dallas' best passer, can start passing to himself."},{"week":6,"rank":7,"record":"14-8","summary":"It's only a bad rumor. Mavs didn't really petition the league to play all their games on the road. Not after slipping to 7-5 at home; not even after winning three straight roadies by 10-plus."},{"week":7,"rank":8,"record":"16-9","summary":"Mavs plagued by inconsistency at PG and C. The problem: Dallas was expecting problems only at PG. Not with Dampier."},{"week":8,"rank":10,"record":"18-10","summary":"From afar, Mavs just watched Nash total at least 10 assists in each game of Suns' 11-game win streak. The same Mavs who have (yikes) one double-digit assist game all season."},{"week":9,"rank":7,"record":"20-10","summary":"Don't forget Dirk, who's right up there with Amare on the list of starry West big man who (regrettably) have no shot at an All-Star start because of the Duncan-Garnett crossfire."},{"week":10,"rank":5,"record":"22-10","summary":"On this five-game homestand, after some serious AAC struggles lately, Dallas is 4-0 and averaging almost 120 points. Imagine if Mavs didn't have PG shortcomings."},{"week":11,"rank":7,"record":"23-12","summary":"A warning: When they visit Charlotte on Friday, Mavs will be outside the state of Texas for the first time since Dec. 26. That game starts a 14-game stretch with 10 roadies for Dallas."},{"week":12,"rank":4,"record":"27-12","summary":"There is no shame ranking No. 2 in Texas these days. Because these Mavs just keep rolling in the face of injuries (Howard, Daniels), surgery (Nellie) and inconsistency (Dampier)."},{"week":13,"rank":6,"record":"28-14","summary":"The good news: Dampier had two double-doubles in three games, on a bad knee. The bad news: Dallas lost both games, including a deflating home defeat to Sixers sans AI."},{"week":14,"rank":5,"record":"31-15","summary":"Nellie returns Tuesday vs. Chicago after Avery's splash as a fill-in, and here's his first task -- Dallas must improve on its dismal 1-5 record vs. Spurs, Suns, Sonics and Kings."},{"week":15,"rank":5,"record":"33-16","summary":"The locals are clamoring for more from Finley, but Mavs couldn't have started the toughest part of their schedule much better, winning at Sacto and Seattle. Could they, Dallasites?"},{"week":16,"rank":2,"record":"35-16","summary":"Every team needs an All-Star break, but if any team didn't want one, it was Dallas after that 4-0 road trip. And Mavs are still waiting to be full strength, which hasn't happened all season."},{"week":17,"rank":4,"record":"37-17","summary":"For much of the season, Dallas' D was actually ahead of its offense. But Van Horn doesn't arrive at the best time; Mavs have allowed 100-plus points in eight of 12."},{"week":18,"rank":6,"record":"38-20","summary":"It's a good thing Mavs are about to see some sub-.500 teams, because they haven't been able to stop anyone with Dampier out -- and Damp could well miss another couple weeks."},{"week":19,"rank":7,"record":"41-21","summary":"Banged-up Mavs have no time to get what their coach says they desperately need. Nellie's view: 'We need 20 games together. . . . We don't even know how to play with each other.'"},{"week":20,"rank":7,"record":"43-22","summary":"Now that the baton has been passed, let's be real. Until Dampier and Stackhouse return, it probably doesn't matter who's coaching. Mavs won't be a factor without those two healthy."},{"week":21,"rank":7,"record":"46-23","summary":"Winner of the Dallas-Sacto season series has lost the teams' last three playoff matchups. So maybe Mavs (3-1 this season) would prefer seeing Houston in Round 1."},{"week":22,"rank":4,"record":"49-24","summary":"You can deal with a lopsided L at Cavs after Ws at Detroit, Boston and Philly -- in the same week Stack and Damp return."},{"week":23,"rank":2,"record":"52-24","summary":"Mavs are becoming a trendy pick to make playoff noise, but more impressive is how steady they've become. This is a fifth straight 50-win season, after just two in the club's first 20 years."},{"week":24,"rank":2,"record":"56-24","summary":"Don't say they have nothing to play for. Those increasingly confident Mavs are trying to finish ahead of Miami ... just in case they need home-court advantage in the Finals."}],"phx":[{"week":1,"rank":8,"record":"3-0","summary":"It took only a week for Suns to supplant Orlando as the league's unofficial bandwagon team. They're scoring freely and racking up fans just as quickly."},{"week":2,"rank":9,"record":"4-2","summary":"Suns feel as though their first 4-0 start since 1984-85 should have been been 6-0, after narrow losses to Cleveland and Sacto. But Outlaw adds a much-needed thirtysomething."},{"week":3,"rank":2,"record":"8-2","summary":"Watch a Suns game this week. Trust us. We could all use a smile and these guys, without doubt, are the league's primo entertainers at present."},{"week":4,"rank":1,"record":"11-2","summary":"You have to go all the way back to 1980-81 to find a Suns team that started this hot (14-2). That's two years before Mr. Stoudemire was born, in case you're wondering."},{"week":5,"rank":3,"record":"14-3","summary":"The reality, Suns fans, is this: Phoenix would have dropped from the top spot even with a win over Minny. Don't be angry with us; San Antonio is simply playing that well."},{"week":6,"rank":2,"record":"17-3","summary":"Things are going so well in the desert that Phoenix has seen two triple-doubles from Kobe -- and won both times. Kobe's career record in triple-double games? 10-2."},{"week":7,"rank":1,"record":"21-3","summary":"Yes, one year (and Nash) makes a big difference. Suns are 10-1 on the road. That's after 10 road wins all last season, and after failing to secure victory No. 21 until March 3, 2004."},{"week":8,"rank":1,"record":"24-3","summary":"Suns' last loss? Try Dec. 3. It therefore shouldn't be a surprise that this is the first team to maintain its hold on the top spot in the rankings since the regular season started."},{"week":9,"rank":3,"record":"26-4","summary":"Amare's 50-pointer was a handy rebound from the SA rout. Suns were safely among the four teams playing .750-or-better ball as of Jan. 1, only the second time in NBA history we've seen that."},{"week":10,"rank":1,"record":"30-4","summary":"What could be sweeter than a return to the top spot? For D'Antoni, it would be coaching the West All-Stars . . . in Denver . . . where he was wrongly dumped by Issel after just one season."},{"week":11,"rank":3,"record":"31-7","summary":"D'Antoni said it best after Nash was so cruelly whacked in the thigh: ''Some people said we needed some adversity to become a good team. Well, there's some adversity for you.''"},{"week":12,"rank":2,"record":"32-10","summary":"The committee, as you know, does not believe in curses. But even we can't deny that the problems in Phoenix appear to have coincided with the release of our ''Sunny and 70'' opus."},{"week":13,"rank":2,"record":"36-10","summary":"What a difference a Nash makes? Suns have topped 120 points 12 times. In the previous seven seasons they did it 10 times."},{"week":14,"rank":2,"record":"38-11","summary":"Knowing Nash, whether or not he gets to start in place of an injured Kobe, he's seriously bummed that D'Antoni won't get to return to Denver as the West's coach."},{"week":15,"rank":1,"record":"40-12","summary":"The bench is filling out, with Wal-tuh joining Jim Jax ... but it's starting to look as though 70 wins is beyond them."},{"week":16,"rank":3,"record":"41-13","summary":"Suns apparently aren't greedy. Team sources say they'll be perfectly happy with any win total in the 60s."},{"week":17,"rank":3,"record":"43-14","summary":"Suns have clearly solved their Can't Score Without Nash problem. But they can't rise higher until he's back in uniform."},{"week":18,"rank":1,"record":"46-14","summary":"No, they're not going to win 70. Or even 69. But with Nash back in the lineup, and after the statement wins over Detroit and Seattle, Suns are on pace to win a healthy 63."},{"week":19,"rank":1,"record":"48-15","summary":"Impressive as it was to see Suns recover from the Houston loss by winning at Denver, Nash's quote after that Rockets defeat is worrisome: 'I'm not helping us very much on one leg.'"},{"week":20,"rank":3,"record":"49-16","summary":"Nash says his hamstring is feeling a little better. Better yet, after a nice win at Memphis, Suns are quietly 8-3 since the All-Star break, beating Spurs, Pistons, Sonics, Mavs and Nuggets."},{"week":21,"rank":1,"record":"52-17","summary":"Suns play 10 of their final 13 games at home. Of course, as good as they are on the road -- leading the league at 29-8 -- maybe that closing sked helps San Antonio more than Phoenix."},{"week":22,"rank":1,"record":"56-17","summary":"The run-and-gunners have scored 120-plus points 18 times. Suns did it only 10 times in the previous seven seasons."},{"week":23,"rank":4,"record":"57-19","summary":"With a series looming against a team (Memphis) they don't like to play, Suns can be thankful for one thing. After two straight L's to GS, at least Suns don't have to see Warriors in Round 1."},{"week":24,"rank":1,"record":"61-19","summary":"So they didn't maintain that 31-4 pace. Big deal. Suns following up that sick start with a 30-15 burst looks quite sufficient."}],"hou":[{"week":1,"rank":9,"record":"2-2","summary":"Perilously close to the first 0-3 start in JVG's coaching career, Rockets eventually emerged from a four games-in-five nights stretch with some style."},{"week":2,"rank":12,"record":"3-4","summary":"Rockets' start was slow before McGrady hurt his hip and/or groin. Hard to see them getting healthy soon, with six of the next seven games on the road."},{"week":3,"rank":15,"record":"6-6","summary":"Perhaps we shouldn't be surprised that they've started slowly. Rockets just might be the slowest team in the league, because of a serious athleticism shortage that must be addressed."},{"week":4,"rank":19,"record":"6-9","summary":"Denver's gradual recovery means that Rockets have launched to the top of the league's Most Disappointing list. It's a state law that every team in Texas should be at least .500."},{"week":5,"rank":22,"record":"7-11","summary":"At Van Gundy's request, T-Mac is vowing to be more aggressive. The real problem in Houston: JVG is hesitant to ask the same from a passive Yao, who also looks tired already."},{"week":6,"rank":17,"record":"9-12","summary":"The flip side to all the T-Mac hubbub: 10 times already, in 19 games, McGrady has scored fewer than 20 points, which happened only 13 times in 67 games last season."},{"week":7,"rank":17,"record":"11-13","summary":"To echo a point made recently on NBA Fastbreak by our pal Ric Bucher, how much better would Houston be right now with Eddie Griffin as an athletic power forward to partner with Yao?"},{"week":8,"rank":18,"record":"13-14","summary":"Even in the unlikely event that Atlanta's Barry does make a big different at the point, Rockets still have PF issues. Yao and T-Mac better start combining for 74 points more often."},{"week":9,"rank":12,"record":"16-15","summary":"With two new guards (J. Barry and Wesley), perhaps now Houston can work on another problem. Like, say, its 6-8 record vs. the East ... compared to 9-7 against the West."},{"week":10,"rank":15,"record":"17-17","summary":"Anyone else feel like Rudy might have been a better coaching fit for the T-Mac-Yao tag team than JVG? Anyone else notice Rudy is 2-0 vs. Rockets and 15-14 otherwise?"},{"week":11,"rank":12,"record":"20-17","summary":"Looks like Houston's roster revamping will deemphasize Yao's role on offense a bit. Which probably isn't the worst idea for a guy who's still only fit enough to play 31 mpg."},{"week":12,"rank":12,"record":"22-19","summary":"It's a safe bet, even with half a season to go, that T-Mac will have no trouble averaging 20 ppg under Van Gundy, as some suggested. T-Mac's at 28.1 ppg over his last 25 games."},{"week":13,"rank":11,"record":"24-21","summary":"Ever since they came to Dallas and posted a 124-point night in the committee's presence, Rockets have scored 100 only twice in the past nine games, going 6-4 in that span."},{"week":14,"rank":7,"record":"28-21","summary":"The only team this season besides Seattle to beat San Antonio twice just completed a 4-0 week, with three of those victories on the road. Looks like they're getting it."},{"week":15,"rank":6,"record":"31-21","summary":"It's a good thing Rockets are so hot -- 15-4 since Jan. 7 -- because our research staff says they have the NBA's toughest remaining schedule based on opponent winning percentage."},{"week":16,"rank":7,"record":"32-21","summary":"An eight-game win streak is encouraging in itself, but then there's this: Yao is quietly averaging 20.5 ppg on 64.5-percent shooting during Houston's 8-0 run. Not bad at all."},{"week":17,"rank":9,"record":"32-24","summary":"Even after trading for Wesley and Jon Barry, formerly scorching Rockets needed to swing a buzzer trade for longtime target Mike James because Sura's back, by all accounts, doesn't look good."},{"week":18,"rank":10,"record":"34-25","summary":"It appears the All-Star break came at the worst time for Rockets, but look at the standings. No. 5 Sacto is well within reach."},{"week":19,"rank":6,"record":"37-25","summary":"Rockets are your proverbial Team O' The Week. Only problem with Houston's surge is that the No. 6 seed might prove more attractive than No. 5, depending on San Antonio's finish."},{"week":20,"rank":8,"record":"39-27","summary":"Rockets haven't been this far over .500 since 1996-97. But they really don't feel like celebrating after losing Juwan for a while."},{"week":21,"rank":5,"record":"42-28","summary":"All Rockets needed to finally seize No. 5 out West was a win over Duncan-less Spurs. Instead Houston joined Atlanta and Charlotte as the only teams to lose to SA with Duncan out."},{"week":22,"rank":9,"record":"44-30","summary":"Just when we were ready to anoint Houston as the Lower Seed No One Wants To Face out West, Rockets played New Orleans at home on April Fool's Day ... and lost. No joke."},{"week":23,"rank":8,"record":"46-31","summary":"The bad news? Rockets are 7-6 since losing Juwan for good. The good news? A win in Monday's road finale at Seattle would make this Houston's second-best road team ever at 25-16."},{"week":24,"rank":7,"record":"49-31","summary":"Postseason success, of course, is what really matters for T-Mac, who has never won a playoff series. But 50 wins would be nice, too. T-Mac's previous teams have never topped 45-37."}],"tor":[{"week":1,"rank":10,"record":"3-0","summary":"Vinsanity and his Raps had a dream week worthy of a massive jump . . . apart from that court ruling which mandates a payment of nearly $5 million to VC's former agent."},{"week":2,"rank":18,"record":"4-3","summary":"Vince's fourth-quarter benchings? Sorry. The obvious question here when Raps started 4-1: How are they doing this without a major contribition from Pape Sow?"},{"week":3,"rank":19,"record":"5-6","summary":"An angry Commish had no real outlet to crack down on Vinsanity for his ludicrous trade request . . . but Coach Mitchell obviously does. We just wish Pape was getting those VC minutes."},{"week":4,"rank":23,"record":"6-9","summary":"As if Coach Mitchell hasn't seen enough already in this debut season -- Pape, too -- Raps play their next six on the road. That doesn't sound good."},{"week":5,"rank":25,"record":"7-12","summary":"Did you notice how quickly Raps went from urging Vince to give the new Babcock-Mitchell regime a chance to granting his wish to try to trade him back to the States?"},{"week":6,"rank":27,"record":"7-16","summary":"Won't go too deep into what VC's injury does to his trade prospects. Because: Isiah wants Vinsanity healthy or not, and we don't like to go more than a week without mentioning Pape."},{"week":7,"rank":26,"record":"9-17","summary":"It's not just us, people. Here's an actual e-mail received by the committee: 'I think it's fairly obvious Vince was traded so Toronto could focus on Pape Sow as its franchise player.' See?"},{"week":8,"rank":25,"record":"10-19","summary":"Raps could really use hockey's return about now to distract the locals from this nagging question: T-Mac and now Vince are gone, and what has this franchise gotten in return?"},{"week":9,"rank":25,"record":"10-21","summary":"You were warned, Raps fans, that rushing into a Vince trade to keep THIS season from fading away made no sense. Agree now?"},{"week":10,"rank":23,"record":"13-22","summary":"Thanks to Raps and their upset of Sacto -- and Charlotte's rout of Minny on the same night -- Eastern Conference teams went 6-0 against the West on Wednesday. For real."},{"week":11,"rank":23,"record":"15-23","summary":"Matt Winer, on NBA Fastbreak, on Toronto's season so far: ''If only they could win in the United States.'' It's true: Raps' Bosh Era would be even better if they could buy a road win."},{"week":12,"rank":20,"record":"18-24","summary":"Now that Bosh, one of our faves, has been established as Le Man in Toronto, the next step is improving the D. Reason being: Raps are 0-19 when they surrender 100 points."},{"week":13,"rank":22,"record":"18-27","summary":"No one in the Atlantic is a road powerhouse, but Raps must be ashamed to know they'd be winning the division if they weren't four wins shy of Boston's 7-16 away record."},{"week":14,"rank":23,"record":"20-28","summary":"After six straight weeks with no Pape references, we couldn't resist. But (I guess) we can understand Raps' reluctance to play him, so long as the playoffs remain a possibility."},{"week":15,"rank":25,"record":"21-31","summary":"Scuffling with Rafer. Wrestling with Vince before the trade. Trade-me complaining from Eric Williams. Mitchell's coaching reign is even rowdier than O'Neill's, isn't it?"},{"week":16,"rank":25,"record":"21-32","summary":"At All-Star Weekend, Vince said we're all making too much of his forthcoming reacquaintance with the Raptors. We're guessing Raps fans don't feel the same way."},{"week":17,"rank":23,"record":"24-32","summary":"Raps' what-next season continues with two surprises -- zero trades at the deadline and a 3-0 week coming out of the break."},{"week":18,"rank":24,"record":"25-34","summary":"The committee is vain enough to think that Raps activated our man Pape just in time for us to see him in person Monday night in Dallas. Go ahead, try convincing us otherwise."},{"week":19,"rank":24,"record":"27-36","summary":"Mo Pete is now the league's reigning Iron Man at 260 consecutive games. Of course, in line with Raps' recent fortunes, you'll note that A.C. Green's record is 1,192 consecutive games."},{"week":20,"rank":24,"record":"28-38","summary":"Raps are 21-24 since trading Vince. Not bad, actually, but not good enough to close all wounds opened by Vince's renaissance."},{"week":21,"rank":24,"record":"29-40","summary":"Attn. folks who don't like our occasional bon mots for Pape: Send suggestions. Toronto is one of our favorite cities, but not much Raps-wise is happening up there these days. Is there?"},{"week":22,"rank":23,"record":"30-43","summary":"People, people, people. Most of your suggestions were Bosh-related, a lefty we love and praise as much as Pape. Pumping Bosh up is nothing new in this cyberspace."},{"week":23,"rank":22,"record":"31-45","summary":"Stuff is happening anew. Bosh is a bit more outspoken, Vince returns to town Friday ... and Pape just got his first NBA start."},{"week":24,"rank":21,"record":"32-48","summary":"If Pape's starting, we'll be watching. We'll also be watching Wednesday's finale to track Cleveland's fate and see two of our favorite lefties for the last time 'til fall: Bosh and Jalen."}],"den":[{"week":1,"rank":11,"record":"1-2","summary":"Even after the comeback win over Minny, this might be the most disappointing team so far. One of the problems: Even K-Mart says his buddy Melo is trying too hard to be great."},{"week":2,"rank":22,"record":"2-5","summary":"Against legit NBA Finals contenders -- Minnesota and Detroit, specifically -- Nuggets are 2-0. The other five games? All losses by double digits."},{"week":3,"rank":14,"record":"5-5","summary":"Nuggets are rebounding when they absolutely have to, in the midst of a 10-game stretch with nine home dates . . . and a seven-game roadie to follow,"},{"week":4,"rank":13,"record":"7-6","summary":"The home-heavy schedule has certainly helped, but it would be just 'Melo's luck for his freshly tweaked ankle to keep him out of Thursday's national TV showdown with LeBron."},{"week":5,"rank":11,"record":"9-7","summary":"The good news: Nuggets have quietly won eight of 11. The bad news: Denver's seven-game, 11-day trip is up next, while the pressure on 'Melo just keeps building."},{"week":6,"rank":11,"record":"12-8","summary":"With four games left on a brutal trip, Nuggets are off to a decent 2-1 start. Of greater promise: 'Melo is starting to look like last year's edition."},{"week":7,"rank":13,"record":"13-11","summary":"If you're keeping score, Nuggets just went 3-4 on their seven-game trip ... and 'Melo has managed to twist both of his ankles inside two months."},{"week":8,"rank":14,"record":"13-14","summary":"Nuggets could use some more steadiness in the New Year. They started off 1-4, then went 11-3 and are presently trying to extricate themselves from a 1-7 slide."},{"week":9,"rank":17,"record":"14-16","summary":"Coop-a-Loop is the first to go from WNBA head coach to NBA boss ... after Frank Layden, Ron Rothstein, Richie Adubato, Darrell Walker and Brian Winters switched the other way."},{"week":10,"rank":21,"record":"14-19","summary":"What makes them so disappointing, besides the far-too-casual attitude seen far too often from them, is Nuggets' porous defense. Not what we expected in the K-Mart Era."},{"week":11,"rank":21,"record":"15-21","summary":"It's not affecting his jersey sales, obviously, but it has to hurt 'Melo that there are at least five guys in front of him for an All-Star reserve slot opposite LeBron in Denver's All-Star Game."},{"week":12,"rank":17,"record":"17-23","summary":"Nuggets have lost nine of 10 on the road. With nine home losses already, that has to change -- no matter how many injuries they have -- if Denver wants to stay in the playoff chase."},{"week":13,"rank":16,"record":"19-25","summary":"Don't forget that, before everything unraveled, Furious George turned Bucks into a playoff team after seven seasons out of the playoffs. So don't be shocked if he turns Denver around, too."},{"week":14,"rank":15,"record":"21-26","summary":"There's a reason Nuggets will keep getting linked with a possible Payton trade: Andre Miller has only five double-digit assists games all season, zero since Karl took over."},{"week":15,"rank":17,"record":"23-28","summary":"They're a solid 6-3 in the Furious George era, but Nuggets will have to improve their road fortunes -- they've lost 14 of 18 roadies -- to make a real push for the 8th seed."},{"week":16,"rank":20,"record":"24-29","summary":"Nuggets were the fifth host in the past six seasons to carry a losing record into All-Star Weekend. Lakers, though, would trade remaining schedules with Nuggets in a heartbeat."},{"week":17,"rank":15,"record":"27-29","summary":"Furious George thinks it'll take 44 wins to secure the No. 8 slot. At his current 10-4 pace, George will get Nuggets to 45-37."},{"week":18,"rank":11,"record":"30-29","summary":"Nuggets have encountered only three better-than-.500 teams in the Furious George era, but let's face it. They were losing to all kinds of opposition, good and bad, before he got there."},{"week":19,"rank":10,"record":"32-30","summary":"Nuggets are winning so much lately, George has little cause to be furious. Sunday's loss to Phoenix -- the second half of a back-to-back -- was the new coach's first home defeat."},{"week":20,"rank":10,"record":"35-30","summary":"Interesting stat: Nuggets now have more wins with Furious George in charge (18) than they had in the first 42 games (17)."},{"week":21,"rank":8,"record":"38-30","summary":"The committee didn't believe it when some of our Nuggets pals said they were gunning for the seventh seed out West. But take a look: Denver is much closer to No. 7 than No. 9."},{"week":22,"rank":5,"record":"41-31","summary":"Throw out their last two games against Phoenix and Furious George has Nuggets on a stunning 17-0 run. Overall they're 14-1 at home for the new coach and 10-5 on the road."},{"week":23,"rank":1,"record":"45-31","summary":"Dare we say it's safe to anoint Denver as the proverbial Lower Seed No One Wants To Play. Nuggets are now  a ridiculous 21-0 since Feb. 23 . . . if you exclude two losses to Phoenix."},{"week":24,"rank":4,"record":"48-32","summary":"We don't want to worry Furious George, but the last team to post the best record after the All-Star break and lose in Round 1 was ... George's 1994 Sonics. To Denver, remember."}],"sac":[{"week":1,"rank":12,"record":"0-3","summary":"Kings have to hope it really is the schedule. They haven't seen a start this ugly since Webber was still a Bullet, Bibby was still an Arizona Wildcat and Peja was still in Greece."},{"week":2,"rank":8,"record":"3-4","summary":"See? Kings' 0-3 start was at least a little bit about their brutal schedule. They look more Kings-like at home and they're hoping Saturday's win at Phoenix will be their road platform."},{"week":3,"rank":6,"record":"6-4","summary":"It sounds as though Peja's Sacto home is no longer for sale . . . and it looks as though Arco is still a place teams would rather not visit. No matter how un-deep the new Kings are."},{"week":4,"rank":6,"record":"8-5","summary":"It's only one home loss, after a 6-0 start, but it's the fourth to Minny (including playoffs) in the teams' past six Arco dates. Does that make it a trend?"},{"week":5,"rank":5,"record":"12-5","summary":"Remember that 0-3 start? From those depths, Kings and their empty bench have quickly climbed within sight (two games) of the Pacific Division lead."},{"week":6,"rank":5,"record":"14-6","summary":"Friday's collapse in Minnesota brought back some bad playoff memories for Sacto, but the fact remains that Kings are 5-1 on the road after their 0-4 road start."},{"week":7,"rank":6,"record":"16-7","summary":"Hate to put a disclaimer on Kings' recovery, but facts is facts: Sac is just 8-7 against West and fattening up (8-0) on the East."},{"week":8,"rank":8,"record":"17-9","summary":"This could be a problem. Kings have handled regular-season injuries better than anyone in the new millennium, but Sac's lack of depth faces a three-month test with B-Jax shelved."},{"week":9,"rank":5,"record":"19-9","summary":"Kings earn another shot at No. 5 by clamping down on Spurs without B-Jax. Quite a big win considering they've already lost four home games, after losing just seven at Arco last season."},{"week":10,"rank":10,"record":"21-11","summary":"As if the Bobby Jax news wasn't depressing enough, losses to Raps and Hornets really put the Kings of Thin in a funk."},{"week":11,"rank":6,"record":"24-11","summary":"Two reasons to like the Christie-Mobley deal better for Sac: Mo Evans has shown enough promise to warrant more minutes, and Petrie hasn't made many bad deals we can remember."},{"week":12,"rank":5,"record":"27-12","summary":"Until Spurs showed up, Sacramento had been unbeaten (6-0) since swapping for Christie for Mobley. Even after Sunday night, Kings are suddenly just two back of Phoenix in the loss column."},{"week":13,"rank":4,"record":"30-13","summary":"Kings have closed the gap on division-leading Suns, but they must fear a re-widening if Webb and Peja stay in street clothes with Bobby Jax ... and with 12 of the next 17 on the road."},{"week":14,"rank":6,"record":"32-15","summary":"First it was Brad Miller, and now Bibby is trying to make West coaches take notice of how he's carrying injury-ravaged Kings."},{"week":15,"rank":8,"record":"33-18","summary":"Sunday's win at Boston was a nice way to cap a challenging week, after losses to Suns, Sonics and Mavs. Kings are now 3-5 since Adelman's contract was extended."},{"week":16,"rank":11,"record":"33-20","summary":"There's a reason so much trade talk is swirling around these guys. Adelman calls Sacto's recent 1-6 slide 'the toughest stretch we've gone through since I've been here.'"},{"week":17,"rank":7,"record":"36-21","summary":"In their final 25 regular-season games without C-Webb before Thursday's trade, Kings went a whopping 21-4. And they haven't looked too shabby since the trade, either."},{"week":18,"rank":8,"record":"37-24","summary":"Kings have been so up-and-down since Webber left that you have to wonder if their Philly win was purely adrenaline-based. They lost at Charlotte a few nights later, remember."},{"week":19,"rank":11,"record":"39-25","summary":"Just when Sacto thought its luck was turning -- with the disputed Bibby buzzer-beater to topple Memphis -- Miller goes down for perhaps the rest of the regular season. A killer blow."},{"week":20,"rank":12,"record":"41-27","summary":"At 7-7 since the Webber deal, and with Miller out now, you have to start wondering if Kings will slip all the way down to No. 7 and into a first-round series against (ugh) Spurs or Suns."},{"week":21,"rank":12,"record":"43-28","summary":"Our money's on Philly for the big Monday night showdown. Can't see Webber losing both games to his old team."},{"week":22,"rank":14,"record":"45-30","summary":"Kings apparently need more games against Philly. They've looked tough both times they saw Webber, but the fact remains that Sac is 13-16 since checking in at 32-14 on Feb. 4."},{"week":23,"rank":10,"record":"48-30","summary":"Peja has picked it up (24.6 ppg in his last nine), and Kings, after looking as though they could drop all the way to No. 7 out West, have averaged 119 points in their last five games."},{"week":24,"rank":12,"record":"49-31","summary":"Wouldn't be Kings playoff season without injuries: B. Miller, B. Jackson and now Peja. Chances are they all play in the playoffs; chances are better none of them will be 100 percent."}],"lal":[{"week":1,"rank":13,"record":"2-2","summary":"Kobe who? Lakers apparently go as Chris Mihm goes. The proof: Shaq's replacement is averaging 21 ppg and 11 rpg in L.A.'s two wins; 7 and 7 in the two losses."},{"week":2,"rank":11,"record":"4-4","summary":"You can feel all alone sometimes carrying these Lakers. Ditto for presenting at the American Music Awards, when the boo-birds sound off unexpectedly."},{"week":3,"rank":11,"record":"6-5","summary":"Interesting point raised by my colleague Greg Anthony, who says Magic got more for T-Mac than Lakers got for Shaq. I'm starting to agree with him? Do you?"},{"week":4,"rank":12,"record":"8-6","summary":"So Mailman's agent says his client won't be back on the floor until January at the earliest. It's safe to say Kobe is willing to wait as long as he needs to for the extra help."},{"week":5,"rank":13,"record":"10-7","summary":"Lakers' start is a tough read, with only two of their wins (over Denver and the crosstown Clips) coming against teams with winning records. And that 1-1 record vs. Chicago doesn't help."},{"week":6,"rank":13,"record":"12-8","summary":"It's the new triangle in L.A., and you're advised against calling it a love triangle: Kobe-Mailman-Shaq. The next week likely belongs to Kobe and Karl until we switch to Kobe vs. Shaq mode."},{"week":7,"rank":12,"record":"13-10","summary":"What do Lakers and Raps have in common? Neither got an All-Star in return when trading a franchise player . . . although Lakers, to be fair, got more than Raps did."},{"week":8,"rank":15,"record":"14-12","summary":"It's hard to believe, but Lakers insist it's true. They say the media turnout for Shaq-Kobe I was only comparable to a second-round playoff game."},{"week":9,"rank":11,"record":"16-12","summary":"Lakers won only one of the first seven games in which Kobe went for 40. Since Christmas, they've won two in a row when he did."},{"week":10,"rank":14,"record":"17-14","summary":"Blame it on the rain? Some of you would undoubtedly rather blame the rain on Kobe. But not us, citing Friday's resolution."},{"week":11,"rank":15,"record":"20-15","summary":"If it's going to take a long-term injury to Kobe to convince Rudy T. to run more of the offense through Odom in the post, then it will be worth whatever suffering awaits LA in the short-term."},{"week":12,"rank":14,"record":"22-16","summary":"Winning without Kobe isn't just admirable -- it's crucial. Because Lakers are scheduled to play 24 of 38 on the road after Feb. 3, which won't be easy even if Kobe is back by then."},{"week":13,"rank":15,"record":"23-19","summary":"It's safe to say they're starting to miss Kobe. New Jersey was the third East team to win at Staples, compared to zero last season."},{"week":14,"rank":16,"record":"24-21","summary":"Laker players would be wise to let all of us focus on the coaching stuff, because they have 23 roadies left and only 14 games at home. In other words, they need Kobe back ASAP."},{"week":15,"rank":18,"record":"25-24","summary":"Going 6-8 without Kobe? Solid. Now that he's back, the bigger problem is still the sked: 33 games to go, 19 of them away."},{"week":16,"rank":18,"record":"26-24","summary":"You have to wonder how the trade rumors will affect Odom's play from here. Because chances are Lakers don't pull off a deal between now and Thursday, for Boozer or anyone else."},{"week":17,"rank":19,"record":"28-26","summary":"Laker Lovers have been unhappy with their team's ranking for weeks. But facts is facts: Lakers are a league-worst 7-18 against the 16 teams that had winning records on Monday morning."},{"week":18,"rank":17,"record":"30-28","summary":"Home wins over Dallas and Indy were musts. Reason being: Thursday starts a closing stretch of 15 roadies in 23 games."},{"week":19,"rank":15,"record":"32-29","summary":"Lakers' playoff chances would have been boosted by a trade at the deadline, but Kobe has scored at least 32 points in five straight. L.A. is 4-1 in those games and, thus, hanging in there."},{"week":20,"rank":20,"record":"32-34","summary":"Orlando was 45-37 in its first season without Shaq. Lakers, presently on a 40-42 pace, would probably make the playoffs if they could somehow match that Magic effort."},{"week":21,"rank":22,"record":"32-37","summary":"Lakers went 6-8 in the 14 games Kobe missed. So you can't suggest that was the stretch that doomed L.A.'s playoff bid, because its 14 games this month have been uglier (4-10)."},{"week":22,"rank":22,"record":"33-40","summary":"Odom's out. Kobe's freshly injured. The schedule won't let up. So it's all but official: Lakers won't be able to avoid just their fourth non-playoff season since moving to L.A. in 1960."},{"week":23,"rank":24,"record":"34-43","summary":"Another fave (L.A. Times' Mark Heisler) points out that Boston ''all but invented this league'' yet hasn't won a title since '86. Meaning you have to be lucky and good to return to glory."},{"week":24,"rank":25,"record":"34-46","summary":"Lakers are actually a robust 27-6 when they hold the opposition under 100 points. Unfortunately there's the small matter of how poorly they defended in those other 47 games."}],"por":[{"week":1,"rank":14,"record":"2-1","summary":"Not trying to be funny, but if Zach can go for 33 and 15 every time, as seen Sunday in Toronto, the new contract recipient should pay his way to fly to every road game."},{"week":2,"rank":19,"record":"3-3","summary":"Looks like Blazers, playoff outsiders coming into the season, will have to rally now just to reclaim Best in the Northwest status, thanks to Seattle's stunning start."},{"week":3,"rank":23,"record":"4-5","summary":"As more than one Blazer has noted, Portland would be No. 1 if these were Clear The Air Rankings. But team meetings don't help you in the NBA Power Rankings unless wins fill the air."},{"week":4,"rank":16,"record":"7-6","summary":"Because the Northwest is the league's toughest division so far, instead of the Southwest as expected, Blazers find themselves -- yikes -- five games back of their regional rivals from Seattle."},{"week":5,"rank":16,"record":"8-8","summary":"Blazers had the league's second-stingiest defense when they woke up Sunday (89.0 ppg). Then Phoenix swept through town and dropped 121 points on them."},{"week":6,"rank":16,"record":"10-9","summary":"This trend will have to change if they hope to make the playoffs in the mighty West: Blazers are 2-6 on the road since winning their road opener at Golden State."},{"week":7,"rank":16,"record":"12-11","summary":"Not a trend they like, since it's probably not a coincidence: Blazers started 10-10 in each of Cheeks' four seasons."},{"week":8,"rank":13,"record":"13-12","summary":"Van Exel is making retirement noises again, and don't forget last season's vow from NVE. The one about retiring unless a Texas team tries to sign him as a free agent this summer."},{"week":9,"rank":19,"record":"14-15","summary":"The speculation about Cheeks' job security is inevitable, but we suspect it's the constant (and unsettling) trade speculation in Portland that contributes to the mediocrity."},{"week":10,"rank":22,"record":"14-18","summary":"Cheeks speculation is the only Blazers speculation to offer these days, and not just because he lost to Lenny in Sunday's Hot Seat Bowl. An injured Reef (elbow) is simply less tradeable."},{"week":11,"rank":22,"record":"15-21","summary":"It had to be the Line O' The Season: 54 points from Stoudamire in Friday's loss to New Orleans ... to go with one assist, zero rebounds and zero turnovers."},{"week":12,"rank":26,"record":"15-24","summary":"Looks like Reef's elbow injury was a bigger blow than expected. Without him, Blazers have lost five straight and nine of 10 to make it 12 losses in 15 games overall."},{"week":13,"rank":23,"record":"17-25","summary":"Our man Stephen A. reports that Cheeks is considering his resignation. After all the chaos he has seen in Portland, the committee (of one) wouldn't blame Cheeks at all."},{"week":14,"rank":22,"record":"20-26","summary":"There's no truth to the rumor Cheeks is trying to win favor with the committee by starting two little lefties together in the backcourt. But we don't deny liking the NVE-Damon combination."},{"week":15,"rank":24,"record":"20-29","summary":"There isn't enough space in this little box to detail all the chaos in Portland. Maybe not even if we used all 30 little boxes."},{"week":16,"rank":21,"record":"21-30","summary":"Tired of the usual chaos? Us, too. So instead we focus on the surging Joel Przybilla, who posted three straight meaty double-doubles before the break. Three!"},{"week":17,"rank":24,"record":"22-32","summary":"Since Blazers didn't join the masses and make a trade, all we can do now is return to the Przybilla Watch."},{"week":18,"rank":25,"record":"22-35","summary":"Couldn't make a real deal at the deadline, in spite of the three expiring contracts (Reef, Van Exel and Damon) on the books, so they apparently decided to trade in the coach instead."},{"week":19,"rank":26,"record":"23-37","summary":"In our ongoing quest to find anything nice to say here, try this: Stoudamire recently became just the second player shorter than 6-0 (after Calvin Murphy) to score 10,000 career points."},{"week":20,"rank":28,"record":"23-41","summary":"Pritchard says he wants to return to personnel work at season's end. Can't blame him: Blazers are 9-27 since a 14-14 start."},{"week":21,"rank":29,"record":"24-44","summary":"Talk about a drought. Blazers don't have a road win over a West foe since (ouch) Opening Night at Golden State."},{"week":22,"rank":29,"record":"24-48","summary":"Some Blazers news, at last, that we're excited to hear: Van Exel, one of our faves, has decided against retiring at season's end."},{"week":23,"rank":27,"record":"25-51","summary":"D. Stoudamire says Blazers losing more than 45 games for the first time since '73-74 feels ''worse'' than embarrassing. Since this isn't an expansion team like his 21-61 rookie-year Raps."},{"week":24,"rank":26,"record":"26-54","summary":"The kiddies' 2-14 mark in March -- the worst month in club history -- has given way to a 2-8 April. At least Portland should get a high draft pick for its season of suffering."}],"mem":[{"week":1,"rank":15,"record":"0-3","summary":"Yikes: Grizz have lost 11 straight if you count the last four games of last season, the first-round series against San Antonio and the suddenly shaky present."},{"week":2,"rank":15,"record":"2-5","summary":"On the worrisome side, $86 million man Pau Gasol is averaging just seven rebounds nightly. On the plus side, we love their new away uniforms."},{"week":3,"rank":16,"record":"4-6","summary":"Grizz is just the fifth 50-win team in history to start the following season 0-4. And now, just when it looked like they were recovering, Pau is freshly hobbled."},{"week":4,"rank":21,"record":"5-9","summary":"Unsolicited advice for Czar Fratello: Cut the 10-man rotation down to eight or nine and try to get Pau and Bonzi on the floor more, for starters."},{"week":5,"rank":21,"record":"6-12","summary":"Word on the street is that The Logo wanted Muss to replace Hubie and ownership wanted The Czar. The key now: Will the players want to listen to either one or, preferably, both?"},{"week":6,"rank":15,"record":"9-13","summary":"The progress is mathematically tangible. Memphis had lost five straight games before Fratello's arrival and is 4-2 since."},{"week":7,"rank":18,"record":"11-15","summary":"The sense remains that Fratello, now 6-4 as Hubie's replacement, won't be the only newcomer. Bonzi especially continues to get peppered with questions about possible trades."},{"week":8,"rank":22,"record":"12-17","summary":"If you're looking for a neato factoid to drop at your next holiday party: Fratello (Hubie) and P.J. Carlesimo (Adelman) are the only coaches ever to replace the same guy with two different teams."},{"week":9,"rank":13,"record":"15-17","summary":"At 10-6 since taking over, and with wins over Detroit and now Minnesota, Czar Fratello has quickly hauled Grizz back into the West's playoff chase. Not even Marv could rip that."},{"week":10,"rank":9,"record":"18-17","summary":"Czar isn't getting the fanfare Hubie got, but we're guessing a New Yorker or two has noticed Fratello's impact in Memphis compared to that of the coach who beat him out in NY."},{"week":11,"rank":9,"record":"20-18","summary":"The only thing not to like about the Czar Fratello era -- with a record of 15-7 and counting -- is the new home unis. Especially compared to those sweet new road unis."},{"week":12,"rank":9,"record":"23-19","summary":"Besides sparking Pau, Czar Fratello has Grizz playing some serious defense as well. In its 9-2 January, Memphis has held eight of 11 opponents under 90 points."},{"week":13,"rank":7,"record":"25-20","summary":"Who needs a second scorer? Memphis is on a 13-3 run even though Pau is Czar Fratello's only player above 12.3 ppg."},{"week":14,"rank":8,"record":"27-21","summary":"Furious George is getting all the fresh pub in Denver, but don't sleep on Czar Fratello, who was 22-28 in his Cleveland farewell (lockout season of '99) ... and who's 22-10 with Grizz."},{"week":15,"rank":9,"record":"30-22","summary":"Czar Fratello is doing just fine, even with Gasol possibly out past the All-Star break, so don't be surprised to see his lead assistant Musselman surface as a Wolves candidate."},{"week":16,"rank":10,"record":"30-23","summary":"Gasol was disappointed but not surprised by the snub. Memphis, after all, has never had an All-Star, and neither did Vancouver."},{"week":17,"rank":11,"record":"31-25","summary":"One of the many reasons no one is excited about seeing Grizz in the first round of the playoffs: Memphis is responsible for two of San Antonio's four home losses since March 1, 2004."},{"week":18,"rank":7,"record":"33-25","summary":"Pau's foot problems somehow haven't slowed Grizz down much. Which only adds to these impressive credentials: Memphis has road wins at Phoenix, San Antonio and Detroit."},{"week":19,"rank":9,"record":"35-27","summary":"How time flies: Gasol hasn't played since Jan. 22. Not sure how long this can last, but credit Grizz -- a gutty 12-8 without him."},{"week":20,"rank":9,"record":"38-28","summary":"Gasol and Bonzi are back, but it's clear that Grizz have an underrated bench and a coach who deserves COY consideration whether or not he has been there all season."},{"week":21,"rank":13,"record":"39-29","summary":"The club record for road wins in a season is 19. But after crashing at home to Hornets, it'll be tough for Grizz to win three more roadies, given their rough remaining schedule."},{"week":22,"rank":13,"record":"41-31","summary":"Swift is out suddenly and might be gone permanently when he hits free agency this summer. Will he be missed? Memphis is 10-8 when he's sidelined and 31-23 when he plays."},{"week":23,"rank":9,"record":"44-32","summary":"Gritty Grizz would have to run the table to match last season's 50 wins. But even if they don't this is the franchise's second-best season by a wide margin over No. 3 (28-54 in '02-03)."},{"week":24,"rank":11,"record":"44-36","summary":"An 0-4 trip means Memphis backed into the playoffs a bit, but don't forget these guys do have road wins over Suns, Pistons and Spurs. Phoenix knows Grizz pose a physical threat."}],"mil":[{"week":1,"rank":16,"record":"1-1","summary":"If Redd and Van Horn can go for 50 a night, like they did against Cleveland, Bucks might be able to cope better than expected without T.J., their little PG."},{"week":2,"rank":16,"record":"3-2","summary":"Mo Williams has been a fine fill-in for T.J. at PG, but that doesn't change the fact that Bucks should be 5-0. Instead they've dropped two heartbreakers to Fla. teams."},{"week":3,"rank":22,"record":"3-5","summary":"As much as we love Redd -- and you know how much that is -- the committee still can't see Bucks finishing higher than fourth in the Central. Even with all Indy's problems."},{"week":4,"rank":24,"record":"4-7","summary":"This is not what Bucks will want to hear, but it's the truth: Even Atlanta has more road wins (one) than they do."},{"week":5,"rank":26,"record":"4-10","summary":"Our man Redd is relieved to be done with Lakers, averaging just 7.0 ppg against Kobe (on 19-percent shooting) instead of his usual 25. But real relief for Bucks would be road win No. 1."},{"week":6,"rank":25,"record":"6-12","summary":"Good thing Bucks finally won a road game. They were halfway to matching the club record for the worst road start to a season; 1976-77's Bucks lost their first 16 away games."},{"week":7,"rank":28,"record":"6-15","summary":"Uh-oh: Bucks have to see Iverson twice more, March 1 and April 18. The same AI who's averaging 47 a game vs. Milwaukee."},{"week":8,"rank":29,"record":"7-16","summary":"The more Bucks lose, the more you expect a Redd trade. Because even if the lefty ace wants to stay, is the Senator going to pay him max dollars to keep this team together?"},{"week":9,"rank":26,"record":"9-18","summary":"At least Bucks haven't lost another point guard. In case you missed our recent discussion on NBA Fastbreak, Milwaukee rebuffed Houston's attempts to trade for James."},{"week":10,"rank":24,"record":"12-19","summary":"The good news: Bucks have won a few lately. The bad news: Jermaine's 55 points followed AI's 54, T-Mac's 42 and Dirk's 39."},{"week":11,"rank":26,"record":"12-22","summary":"It's very sad, but true: Bucks feared deep down that there was no chance Ford could come back this season. Here's hoping they don't have to be so pessimistic next season."},{"week":12,"rank":23,"record":"15-24","summary":"In the NBA's new what-if game, Bucks would only be three games out of first place if they were playing in the Atlantic Division. As it stands, they're 2-0 against Detroit."},{"week":13,"rank":26,"record":"15-27","summary":"Not really sure why Kukoc trade rumors persist. Bucks should probably think about keeping him for the rest of the season; they're 7-2 when Toni plays 10 minutes or more."},{"week":14,"rank":24,"record":"17-28","summary":"It's getting to the point when a good day is simply getting through 24 hours without a new Redd rumor."},{"week":15,"rank":21,"record":"20-28","summary":"It's a little late for a rally ... or is it? Bucks have won three straight and five of six and, as a result, find themselves a mere 3 1/2 games out of the No. 8 spot in the East."},{"week":16,"rank":24,"record":"20-30","summary":"It'll be a long week for Redd fans, but it's highly unlikely Bucks would trade him before the summer. Not unless Redd says he intends to leave in free agency, which he won't say this week."},{"week":17,"rank":21,"record":"23-31","summary":"History told us Redd was not going to be traded before the deadline. Only once in the past 20 years has a guy scoring 23 ppg been dealt at the February buzzer: Dominique in 1994."},{"week":18,"rank":21,"record":"24-33","summary":"Besides Detroit, Bucks are the league's only team to improve their record every month. Month-by-month, Milwaukee is 4-8, 5-9, 6-10 and 8-4 . . . but off to a 1-2 start in March."},{"week":19,"rank":23,"record":"25-36","summary":"The month basically breaks down this way so far: Redd hasn't missed much; Bucks haven't defended much."},{"week":20,"rank":23,"record":"27-38","summary":"Life on the road is as big an issue as any. Milwaukee is just 7-25 in away games, with all seven wins coming against East foes."},{"week":21,"rank":26,"record":"27-42","summary":"After an 0-5 trip, Bucks are relieved to be home for eight of the last 13 games. Then they start sweating Redd's free agency."},{"week":22,"rank":26,"record":"28-45","summary":"Word is that Porter is next in line on the Endangered Coaches List. The local paper, in fact, offers a poll asking fans if the coach should be brought back for a third season."},{"week":23,"rank":25,"record":"29-47","summary":"A long season has the potential to get longer. On April 18, Bucks must face Iverson one last time ... after surrendering at least 40 points to AI each of the first three times."},{"week":24,"rank":23,"record":"30-50","summary":"Does anyone remember that Bucks' season started 3-1? It certainly didn't help that Milwaukee, amid increasing sale and Redd's Leaving speculation, went 0-15 on the road vs. the West."}],"orl":[{"week":1,"rank":17,"record":"2-1","summary":"It could be worse, Orlando. Much, much worse than losing to Charlotte. Remember last season? Magic won on opening night . . . then dropped 19 straight."},{"week":2,"rank":17,"record":"4-3","summary":"Magic thinks it should be better than one game over .500, but you won't hear much complaining because all of Orlando remembers how it feels to go 0-14 in November."},{"week":3,"rank":13,"record":"6-3","summary":"Keep it going, Grant. You sense that everyone associated with the league welcomes any feel-good story it can find right about now and this is clearly No. 1 on the list."},{"week":4,"rank":11,"record":"8-4","summary":"Magic might sit only second in the Southeast, but before Miami's win over Boston on Sunday night, Orlando was (if only briefly) No. 1 in Florida and the division."},{"week":5,"rank":10,"record":"11-5","summary":"Seeing Magic atop the East standings is the last thing T-Mac needed, but it's not just Grant Hill's doing. Orlando also tops the league in rebound margin at (wow) nearly plus-5 per game."},{"week":6,"rank":9,"record":"13-7","summary":"Is the rookie rebounding machine starting to slowing down? Howard has been held below 10 boards four times in December already, and that happened only twice in all of November."},{"week":7,"rank":10,"record":"14-10","summary":"Okafor might have seized the ROY lead from Howard, but Magic still share the second-best start in the East. Which means something after last winter."},{"week":8,"rank":5,"record":"15-10","summary":"This is out-of-control high for the Magic, honestly, but the committee is having real issues these days after No. 4 with only four teams in the whole league on any kind of run."},{"week":9,"rank":16,"record":"15-13","summary":"Thank you, Magic, for teasing the committee with that Spurs win ... and then shaming us vs. Knicks, Bucks and Bulls after we gambled on your promotion. Another No. 5 bites the dust."},{"week":10,"rank":12,"record":"18-14","summary":"Good luck trying to get a read on these guys. Promoted to No. 5, beaten by four straight stragglers and then victorious in a rout over Seattle. Thanks yet again, Magic."},{"week":11,"rank":13,"record":"20-16","summary":"If Stevie Franchise is going to miss Mobley as much as he says, the trade was a must. He really needs to toughen up."},{"week":12,"rank":13,"record":"22-17","summary":"When they've won lately, Magic's wins have been good ones: Minnesota, Indiana, Detroit. Orlando's 11-6 record against the West, furthermore, is still the East's best."},{"week":13,"rank":12,"record":"24-19","summary":"Stevie Franchise prefers to be called Steve-O now. Isn't Matt Winer's NBA Fastbreak nickname better: Stevie New Franchise?"},{"week":14,"rank":12,"record":"25-22","summary":"It's safe to say Magic have noticed that, in spite of Boston's recent surge, they'd be in first place by a game and a half if they didn't get relocated to the Southeast."},{"week":15,"rank":13,"record":"27-24","summary":"The honeymoon might be ending. Stevie New Franchise criticized his teammates; GM Weisbrod challenged his coach; and Dwight Howard slipped behind Ben Gordon in the ROY race."},{"week":16,"rank":13,"record":"28-24","summary":"Magic still boasts an encouraging 13-9 record against the West, but -- besides the latest Francis flap -- Orlando's 9-18 road mark is No. 8 on the East's list of 10 playoff contenders."},{"week":17,"rank":17,"record":"28-27","summary":"Is it just us or does the Grant Hill fairy tale suddenly look like it won't last beyond the regular season? If anyone in the East's top eight seems vulnerable to a slide these days, it's Orlando."},{"week":18,"rank":14,"record":"31-27","summary":"Just like the last time Magic took a steep dip, way back in Week 9, they rallied with a win streak. Johnny Davis needed that."},{"week":19,"rank":16,"record":"31-31","summary":"Heartwarming as it would be to see Grant Hill back on the playoff stage, Orlando's ongoing struggles are actually the biggest source of postseason hope in Philly and Indy these days."},{"week":20,"rank":19,"record":"32-34","summary":"Francis. Augmon. Weisbrod v. T-Mac. A coaching change. Things are unraveling so fast for this former feel-good team and poor Grant Hill that you don't know where to start."},{"week":21,"rank":21,"record":"32-37","summary":"It's one thing if you fire a coach in March and you have Brendan Malone to take over. It's another when Johnny Davis, like him or not, is replaced by someone with no experience."},{"week":22,"rank":20,"record":"35-38","summary":"Maybe the unraveling is subsiding, although we suspect that Saturday's victory in Jersey did more to hurt Nets' playoff bid than help a Magic team missing Hill, Hedo and Jameer."},{"week":23,"rank":20,"record":"35-41","summary":"These guys are tough to console with Hill and Hedo out and the playoffs all but gone, but no one can take away Orlando's more-than-respectable record of 15-15 against the West."},{"week":24,"rank":22,"record":"35-45","summary":"Like Frank Hamblen says to all moms: ''Don't let your sons grow up to be interim coaches.'' Injury-ravaged Magic are 4-12 under Jent after losing six straight before he took over."}],"phi":[{"week":1,"rank":18,"record":"1-2","summary":"The Answer is telling anyone who'll listen how much he likes Coach Obie. To this point, though, all they have is each other, which ain't nearly enough."},{"week":2,"rank":14,"record":"4-3","summary":"It's early, true, but AI is making big shots and fancy passes with regularity. If his ankle is an issue, it's tough to tell."},{"week":3,"rank":21,"record":"4-6","summary":"Belated disclaimer on last Wednesday's praise of AI the PG: AI has to be playing for the praise to apply, but a sore elbow shelved him Sunday."},{"week":4,"rank":20,"record":"6-7","summary":"Anyone else sense that Obie isn't thrilled with Philly's early play? Except for AI, the new coach has tried at least two different starters at every position."},{"week":5,"rank":23,"record":"6-10","summary":"Tuesday's visit to lowly Atlanta is a serious opportunity for Sixers. That's because Philly has lost seven straight road games since an Opening Night victory at Boston."},{"week":6,"rank":22,"record":"8-12","summary":"Can't agree with O'Brien's issues with Dalembert, but credit the new coach for reaching Iverson. AI first spoke out on O'Brien's behalf, then scored 40 points for him on a winning Sunday."},{"week":7,"rank":21,"record":"10-13","summary":"Good thing AI is scorching hot, because O'Brien doesn't seem to have confidence in anyone else. Seven different Sixers have been benched for at least one game, including Dalembert."},{"week":8,"rank":23,"record":"11-14","summary":"Sixers have to be relieved that Iverson, at 29 and with that four-year extension kicking in next season, looks as deadly as ever. Because it's the only thing going right for them."},{"week":9,"rank":22,"record":"13-16","summary":"AI-Kobe comparisons are in circulation for a reason: Iverson led the league, entering the weekend, by attempting 27.4 percent of his team's shots. Kobe is second at 27.1 percent."},{"week":10,"rank":18,"record":"15-17","summary":"As long as AI ain't hurt seriously, these are good times in Philly. Only three other teams in the past 10 seasons have posted a winning record on an eight-game trip like Sixers did at 5-3."},{"week":11,"rank":20,"record":"16-20","summary":"Iverson, at 29, has given us no cause to worry about how he'll hold up at 30. Durability is not the issue in Philly -- as always, it's finding the right guys to play alongside AI."},{"week":12,"rank":18,"record":"18-21","summary":"Eagles? We were under the impression it was a Sixers town, since they're in first place and all."},{"week":13,"rank":19,"record":"20-23","summary":"After 15 of 19 on the road, 24 of their final 39 games are at home. Which might make Sixers the new Atlantic favorites."},{"week":14,"rank":19,"record":"22-24","summary":"Sixers are getting closer, but they still haven't seen .500 since Nov. 26 (6-6) and haven't been above .500 since 4-3."},{"week":15,"rank":16,"record":"25-26","summary":"We picked Boston to win the division, and we're not changing that pick. But how can you not pick AI to win the scoring title?"},{"week":16,"rank":17,"record":"26-27","summary":"Something else to watch for in the season's final third besides what we addressed Monday: Iverson is only three double-digit assist games short of tying his single-season career-high of 18."},{"week":17,"rank":13,"record":"26-29","summary":"Making the Webber deal work, and rallying Philly to win the division, figures to change our stance on AI's MVP-worthiness."},{"week":18,"rank":13,"record":"29-30","summary":"It certainly hasn't been a seamless start for the Iverson-Webber tag team, but the crisis tone is misplaced. Philly has won three of four entering Monday's big test at Miami."},{"week":19,"rank":17,"record":"30-33","summary":"Webber's taking the heat, but it's Iverson's MVP campaign that'll take the big hit if Sixers miss out on the playoffs."},{"week":20,"rank":17,"record":"32-34","summary":"Our man Stephen A. has put the heat squarely on Coach O'Brien. But perhaps this thumb injury is just the sort of bizarro-world spark Iverson needs to carry Philly into the playoffs."},{"week":21,"rank":16,"record":"35-34","summary":"Why all the gloom and doom? Philly's on a 6-2 surge, with a 3½-game lead on the only team that can really catch up (Nets)."},{"week":22,"rank":18,"record":"36-37","summary":"The pressure's on AI, and not just because of Webb's shoulder. This could be the first time since '76-77 that the league's top two scorers (AI and Kobe) miss the playoffs."},{"week":23,"rank":14,"record":"39-37","summary":"Iverson has essentially clinched the scoring title, but this is still a big week for Sixers with games against the team they're chasing (home to Celtics) and the team chasing them (at Nets)."},{"week":24,"rank":14,"record":"41-39","summary":"As promised Friday, Iverson will get LeBron's spot on our MVP ballot and our All-NBA first team if Sixers make it and Cavs miss out. Which looks like a lock now, doesn't it?"}],"okc":[{"week":1,"rank":19,"record":"2-1","summary":"Looks like that 30-point loss to Clips on Opening Night -- which quickly sparked whispers about Coach McMillan's immediate future -- was a really loud wake-up call."},{"week":2,"rank":10,"record":"6-1","summary":"Remember last November, when Flip Murray was deified? Danny Fortson is this season's Flip, because some Sonics fans are apparently calling Fortson the next Lonnie Shelton."},{"week":3,"rank":7,"record":"9-2","summary":"Sayeth Ray: 'I'm not playing like this because it's the last year of my contract.' Sayeth us: The contract issue can't hurt and should help Allen keep this up, even if other Sonics can't."},{"week":4,"rank":3,"record":"13-2","summary":"Don't be smug, Seattle. Surely you didn't expect your Supes to be the first team to reach 10 wins -- or to rank third in the NBA in rebounding differential after a month."},{"week":5,"rank":4,"record":"15-3","summary":"It's only a bad rumor. Sonics didn't really petition the league to play all 82 games this November. They're even off to an encouraging 2-0 start in December."},{"week":6,"rank":1,"record":"17-4","summary":"Here's another way to break it down: Sonics are indeed 0-2 against Boston ... but also 2-0 against San Antonio. You can guess which resonates most with the committee."},{"week":7,"rank":3,"record":"18-5","summary":"It's an Adam Sandler line we can't hear enough, and we're a little late with it as it is, but here goes: Happy Hanukkah to the owner of Seattle SuperSonic-ahs ... past and present."},{"week":8,"rank":2,"record":"19-5","summary":"It's not as good as Sandler and his SuperSonic-ahs, but it's my second-favorite Seattle line: Ray Ray calling the offense 'organized confusion.' One of the lines of the season so far."},{"week":9,"rank":4,"record":"22-6","summary":"The other leading surprise package, along with Phoenix, just completed a restful stretch of one game game in nine days between Dec. 18-26. January will be a lot busier (and tougher)."},{"week":10,"rank":3,"record":"24-8","summary":"More credit where it's overdue: Seattle is now 2-0 against Miami and San Antonio. Makes it easy for Supes to get over that first (two-game) losing streak of the season."},{"week":11,"rank":2,"record":"27-9","summary":"The good news: Sonics have six victories since Dec. 1 in which they've trailed in the fourth quarter. The bad news: Seattle still can't figure out how to beat Clips in L.A."},{"week":12,"rank":3,"record":"28-11","summary":"Sources say Sonics are petitioning the league for more Sunday home games, because they haven't lost one yet (6-0). On the flip side, Seattle is just 11-8 since that 17-3 start."},{"week":13,"rank":3,"record":"30-12","summary":"The good news: Karl's arrival in Denver means the list of teams that can woo Ray away just got one shorter. The bad news: Ray says his uncertain future is starting to be a distraction."},{"week":14,"rank":3,"record":"32-13","summary":"Sonics have to hold firm up here, with a fat division lead and a 7-2 record vs. Spurs, Suns, Kings, Mavs and Heat."},{"week":15,"rank":2,"record":"35-14","summary":"January (8-7) wasn't super, but Supes are a sparkling 5-1 in February and 9-3 overall against .640-or-better teams, even after losing at home Sunday to Dallas."},{"week":16,"rank":5,"record":"35-15","summary":"So how soon do Supes clinch the division? Can they actually clinch before April? Not impossible, if our math is right."},{"week":17,"rank":5,"record":"38-16","summary":"As poorly as they played in Milwaukee, Sonics enjoyed a fine February. They went 8-3, after an 8-7 mark in January."},{"week":18,"rank":3,"record":"41-17","summary":"Can't beat Phoenix on their home floor, but you can forgive Sonics for that. They're still a tidy 7-4 vs. the rest of the top six."},{"week":19,"rank":4,"record":"42-19","summary":"Winning at MSG salvaged something from what had to be Sonics' worst week of the season. Holding a 10 1/2-game division lead over Denver doesn't hurt, either."},{"week":20,"rank":5,"record":"45-20","summary":"Trust us: Coach McMillan is far more concerned about the injury loss of Radmanovic than reports of the season's first locker-room grumbling about minutes, roles, shots, etc."},{"week":21,"rank":4,"record":"48-21","summary":"As hot as Nuggets are, look at Sonics' division lead. It's still nearly 10 games, in spite of stubborn Seattle's recent turmoil."},{"week":22,"rank":6,"record":"50-23","summary":"Wondering what keeps Sonics up here? Slump or not, injuries or not, Sonics are still 23-14 against .500-plus teams, second only to San Antonio's 26-14. Phoenix is third at 24-15."},{"week":23,"rank":11,"record":"50-26","summary":"This is no joke. Sonics haven't won since April 1 and have nothing but injuries (Rashard, Radmanovic, Daniels, Fortson)."},{"week":24,"rank":8,"record":"52-28","summary":"It wasn't the smoothest divisional clinch, but c'mon. Fifty-two wins! Nate must have done some coaching to coax 52 wins out of a smallish squad universally picked to be a doormat."}],"was":[{"week":1,"rank":20,"record":"2-1","summary":"To start 2-0, with their top three big men (Kwame, Haywood, Etan Thomas) either injured or suspended, Wiz earned Team of the Week consideration, too."},{"week":2,"rank":23,"record":"3-4","summary":"Bursting the bubble of a Week 1 overachiever is not something we look forward to (that much), but 3-4 should feel more Wiz-like . . . with only two .500-or-better seasons in the last 17."},{"week":3,"rank":20,"record":"5-4","summary":"The way Wiz season has started, and given how Golden State's season has started, it probably won't be long before Warriors ask for Jamison, Arenas and Hughes to come back."},{"week":4,"rank":18,"record":"7-5","summary":"Here's wishing Coach Jordan a speedy recovery. Wiz are giving up a lot of points, but they're scoring lots, too, making this surprising start too good to miss."},{"week":5,"rank":14,"record":"10-5","summary":"The schedule hasn't been the toughest, true, but 10 wins this early is still an achievement. Last season, Wiz didn't see win No. 10 until Jan. 10, when they improved to 10-25."},{"week":6,"rank":12,"record":"12-6","summary":"Normally we'd have lots to say about the latest Kwame crisis. But it doesn't seem appropriate with Wiz and their Golden State Alumni Association winning so regularly."},{"week":7,"rank":11,"record":"13-9","summary":"As much as Wiz would love to make a rare playoff appearance, they don't want to see Miami if they get there. The season series is already over and Washington went 0-4."},{"week":8,"rank":11,"record":"14-11","summary":"With Crawford down in NY, Arenas-Hughes is suddenly running as the league's undisputed No. 1 backcourt in terms of point production. It's a tad misleading, but Wiz'll take it."},{"week":9,"rank":14,"record":"16-13","summary":"While encouraged by their 7-8 road record, compared to 8-33 last season, Wiz are quite happy to be home now until Jan. 14."},{"week":10,"rank":8,"record":"19-13","summary":"A trio of interviews on NBA Nation. A spanking of Seattle on TNT. Call it the best Wiz week in years. Who needs MJ?"},{"week":11,"rank":8,"record":"22-13","summary":"Things were going too well, obviously. Wiz haven't been this far over .500 since 1979, so inevitably something harsh had to happen. But we'll delay the drop as long as we can."},{"week":12,"rank":8,"record":"24-15","summary":"Not only are Wiz hanging tough without Hughes, but don't forget that they still haven't been able to play Etan and Kwame together because one or the other has always been hurt."},{"week":13,"rank":13,"record":"26-17","summary":"The eight-game home winning streak is gone, and they've taken a dip, but Wiz are hanging in without Hughes (4-4). And Arenas' All-Star case only gets stronger."},{"week":14,"rank":11,"record":"27-19","summary":"You want weird? Since Hughes went down, Washington is actually scoring almost one point more per game (nearly 103 ppg) and shooting the 3 better (up to 37 percent from 34)."},{"week":15,"rank":10,"record":"30-20","summary":"More kudos bound for the nation's capital: Wiz lead the league with 13 victories this season when trailing after three quarters."},{"week":16,"rank":12,"record":"30-22","summary":"It has been a storybook season so far -- including a dreamy weekend for Arenas and Jamison -- but it's getting to the point Wiz need Hughes back if they hope to claim a top-four slot."},{"week":17,"rank":14,"record":"31-24","summary":"Hughes still hasn't played since Jan. 15. The good news? Wiz are a passable 9-11 without him and remain just a half-game out in the chase for the East's No. 4 seed."},{"week":18,"rank":9,"record":"33-25","summary":"Wiz have won nine of their past 10 games when Hughes is in the lineup, and their friendly (re: soft) remaining schedule makes claiming the No. 4 seed a strong possibility."},{"week":19,"rank":12,"record":"33-27","summary":"Only six teams in the East have winning records against the West. And Wiz (12-11) are one of them, behind only Miami (15-10), Detroit (15-10) and Orlando (14-10)."},{"week":20,"rank":11,"record":"36-28","summary":"With six of seven on the road and Jamison ailing, Wiz face the threat of joining Cleveland, Chicago and Orlando on the slide."},{"week":21,"rank":11,"record":"38-30","summary":"Looks like they got the right Jordan this time. Eddie likely won't win Coach of the Year, but he has Wiz off to a 2-2 start on a crucial five-game trip ... without the injured Jamison."},{"week":22,"rank":11,"record":"41-31","summary":"If healthy, Wiz have the playoff capacity to entertain if nothing else. Arenas-Jamison-Hughes ranks as the NBA's highest scoring trio by five points over Amare-Marion-Johnson."},{"week":23,"rank":16,"record":"41-35","summary":"After four 43-point games, Arenas finally reached 44. Problem is, Wiz are 1-4 in those five games, so they need to get back to balance if they want to do something in the playoffs."},{"week":24,"rank":16,"record":"45-35","summary":"References to '97-98 don't apply to Bulls only. Until now, Wiz haven't had a winning season since His Airness retired, either."}],"cle":[{"week":1,"rank":21,"record":"0-3","summary":"No worries about a sophomore jinx for LBJ. The worrisome part is that they're going to miss Boozer even more than they thought if the other Cavs keep playing like this."},{"week":2,"rank":13,"record":"3-3","summary":"The rally against Phoenix was huge for LBJ and his Cavs, even if Amare wasn't on the floor, because it was the sort of game (a close one) last season's squad always lost."},{"week":3,"rank":12,"record":"6-4","summary":"With only one quality win (Phoenix), it's too early to gush over anything here apart from LeBron. Of course, dealing strictly with LeBron you can gush away."},{"week":4,"rank":9,"record":"9-4","summary":"From Dept. O' The Bizarre: Only three teams ever have won five straight after an 0-3 start, and two of them come from Cleveland. That would be 1999's Cavs and current Cavs."},{"week":5,"rank":8,"record":"11-6","summary":"We still don't see LeBron winning the MVP trophy this season, given how Garnett and Duncan are playing, but he sure looks like the best player in the East. Agreed?"},{"week":6,"rank":10,"record":"12-8","summary":"The real reason Gund wants to sell? Because Cavs were the first team since Air Jordan's retirement in 1998 to let Chicago score at least 26 points in all four quarters."},{"week":7,"rank":9,"record":"14-10","summary":"If there was any doubt before, it's gone now: Silas is a McInnis guy. And the coach, according to team sources, has been down on Snow for a while."},{"week":8,"rank":9,"record":"16-11","summary":"So much for the pre-season supposition that McInnis and Snow couldn't co-exist in Cavsland. It's Silas and Snow; Shaq ain't the only one who hasn't buried the hatchet."},{"week":9,"rank":10,"record":"17-12","summary":"The birthday bash, courtesy of Mutombo, threatens to drop Cavs, but LeBron also just reminded us that he's one of only three teenagers in history to score 40 in a game."},{"week":10,"rank":7,"record":"20-12","summary":"That mask is really slowing LeBron down, huh? Meanwhile, in other fashion news, those retro unis with the horizontal pattern somehow look slimming on Tractor Traylor, don't they?"},{"week":11,"rank":10,"record":"22-14","summary":"To all who've asked why Detroit is always ahead of Cleveland, here's the answer: Thursday. Big game, national TV, Kobe exits early ... and still Cavs stumble at statement time."},{"week":12,"rank":7,"record":"24-15","summary":"LeBron's dream is averaging a triple-double some day, like he says in the commercial. But two in one week and a 3-3 trip out West ain't bad for a second-year manchild."},{"week":13,"rank":10,"record":"26-17","summary":"LBJ is an unquestioned MVP candidate. The questionable part is Cavs' lack of quality wins -- beating Memphis was their first W over a .500-or-better team since before Christmas."},{"week":14,"rank":10,"record":"27-19","summary":"So, East coaches, tell us: Do you regret leaving LeBron off last February's All-Star roster yet?"},{"week":15,"rank":11,"record":"29-20","summary":"For some reason, we kind of miss the mask. But it doesn't really matter to LeBron, who has been deadly lately under any circumstances: 27.8 ppg and 9.6 apg in his last nine games."},{"week":16,"rank":9,"record":"30-21","summary":"Redd isn't coming to Cleveland this week -- sorry. But Cavs are still trying to find a shooter before Thursday's deadline."},{"week":17,"rank":10,"record":"31-23","summary":"Two factors have kept Cleveland out of the exalted top six. Cavs are a mere 10-14 against the 16 teams with winning records -- and, worse, have lost six straight road games."},{"week":18,"rank":16,"record":"31-27","summary":"New owner Dan Gilbert is still waiting for his first win. Which means Silas, for the first time since going to Cleveland, is facing some real pressure as Cavs continue to swoon."},{"week":19,"rank":14,"record":"33-27","summary":"After halting that six-game skid by pounding Orlando and Indiana, Cavs (their fans, actually) face the prospect of another letdown Tuesday if Boozer isn't in the building."},{"week":20,"rank":18,"record":"34-30","summary":"This probably isn't the week that pressure will ease on anyone in Cleveland. Cavs could be flirting with .500 after a home date with Detroit and trips to Houston and Dallas."},{"week":21,"rank":17,"record":"35-32","summary":"Cavs haven't won a road game, for any coach, since Jan. 22. And none of the 10 teams they've beaten on the road -- not one -- has had a winning record when the game was played."},{"week":22,"rank":16,"record":"38-34","summary":"One overlooked factor that led to the coaching change: Silas came to Cleveland promising second-half surges from his teams ... but Cavs faded in both of his seasons."},{"week":23,"rank":18,"record":"39-37","summary":"Of all their many issues, nothing is stranger than McInnis falling in and out (and back in) favor. When Cavs just missed last season's playoffs, McInnis' injury was seen as the killer blow."},{"week":24,"rank":20,"record":"40-40","summary":"Gone might be Cavs' first winning record since '97-98. LeBron's Cavs now face becoming just the second team in history to drop out of the playoffs from 10 games over .500 after 50 games."}],"bos":[{"week":1,"rank":22,"record":"1-2","summary":"Unless they start holding leads when they get them, Celts won't allow us to reference the Sox and Patriots very often. Those teams do, and this team hasn't shown it can."},{"week":2,"rank":20,"record":"3-2","summary":"This is probably one of those first-month quirks, but Celts have one of the league's stingiest defenses so far, at 86.6 ppg allowed. Agreed . . . chances are it won't last."},{"week":3,"rank":17,"record":"4-4","summary":"Sonics were due for a loss, true, but Celts were due for a complete game, too. Fact is, Boston's record should be much better, having blown late leads in all its losses."},{"week":4,"rank":22,"record":"4-8","summary":"The only solace for the team that keeps losing close games -- and for those who picked Boston to win the Atlantic -- is that no one in the division has a winning record."},{"week":5,"rank":18,"record":"7-9","summary":"The Pierce-Rivers blowup got all the attention, but the bigger development is Boston finally winning a couple close games (Milwaukee, Toronto) after blowing several late leads."},{"week":6,"rank":20,"record":"8-11","summary":"Even in a division that threatens to offer zero winning teams, winning the Atlantic won't be easy for Celts (still our pick). Especially with no games left against Seattle."},{"week":7,"rank":15,"record":"11-12","summary":"The defense has faded, as predicted, but Celts are finally starting to win the close games. They're up to 5-6 in games decided by three points or fewer (or overtime)."},{"week":8,"rank":12,"record":"12-14","summary":"As Celts continue to chase that elusive .500 record, indications are that Ainge isn't willing to deal Payton right now. But that could change as February approaches."},{"week":9,"rank":18,"record":"13-17","summary":"The hate e-mail piled up when we said Boston's stingy defense early wouldn't last. To wit, our Atlantic favorites have allowed at least 100 points in 11 straight games."},{"week":10,"rank":20,"record":"15-19","summary":"Ouch. Hate to do this to our man Doc Rivers, but he's the first Celtics coach to see his Cs surrender 100 points in 11 consecutive games since (yikes) M.L. Carr in 1997."},{"week":11,"rank":18,"record":"17-20","summary":"A 41-41 finish in his first Orlando season won Doc Rivers a Coach of the Year trophy. A 41-41 record this season would probably make Rivers' Cs runaway Atlantic winners."},{"week":12,"rank":19,"record":"18-22","summary":"When we picked Celts to win the Atlantic, the idea was they'd be getting something -- anything -- from Blount up front. Is it too late to hop on the Al Jefferson bandwagon?"},{"week":13,"rank":18,"record":"21-23","summary":"Patriots? We were under the impresssion it was a Celtics town, since they're in first place and all."},{"week":14,"rank":17,"record":"24-24","summary":"They're not the Patriots yet -- or the Red Sox -- but life ain't so bad after three straight road wins, five straight wins at Minnesota and a leap to .500 for the Atlantic leaders."},{"week":15,"rank":15,"record":"26-26","summary":"With the exile of I Love Wal-tuh (we feel for you, Tommy), Ainge has now changed almost the entire roster. Pierce and Blount are the only holdovers from the last regime."},{"week":16,"rank":14,"record":"27-26","summary":"If they can survive six games out of seven against West foes, Celtics' remaining schedule is as favorable as Philadelphia's. Which means Boston should hang onto its Atlantic lead."},{"week":17,"rank":12,"record":"29-28","summary":"Even Celtics fans we know are calling him Danny Strainge after the 'Toine re-acquisition. But, last we checked, the division lead is still Boston's and Cs have actually gained ground."},{"week":18,"rank":12,"record":"31-29","summary":"With their Glove back, you'd have to say Danny Strainge, er, Ainge is a big Trade Deadline Winner ... if Doc can keep Pierce, 'Toine, GP and Ricky all on the same page."},{"week":19,"rank":8,"record":"34-29","summary":"The defense can still be disappointing, but the numbers don't lie: Celts are 7-1 (and surging) since 'Toine's return."},{"week":20,"rank":6,"record":"38-29","summary":"Ricky Ricky is making a serious Sixth Man push. And Celts can't stop winning, even though they guard almost no one."},{"week":21,"rank":10,"record":"38-32","summary":"This might be an omen. The same week word leaks out that Celts want to add some black to their unis next season, they drop three straight and anger their coach with their cockiness."},{"week":22,"rank":15,"record":"39-34","summary":"If you got excited about the 11-1 start to the latest 'Toine Era (and we did) you have to be concerned by the 1-5 stumble since. And we are, especially now that 'Toine is hurt as well."},{"week":23,"rank":13,"record":"41-35","summary":"Peter May of the Boston Globe makes his usual strong case about Ricky Ricky playing too many minutes to be a true sixth man, but we still feel Davis hasn't received sufficient props."},{"week":24,"rank":10,"record":"45-35","summary":"The reward for Boston's first division crown since '91-92 looks like a first-round series with Indy for the third successive spring. Don't know that we'd call it a welcome reward, though."}],"lac":[{"week":1,"rank":23,"record":"2-1","summary":"Props to Dunleavy, who is stubborn enough to believe Clips -- even after their Kobe heartbreak -- can do more than just beat fellow West stragglers Seattle and Golden State."},{"week":2,"rank":21,"record":"4-3","summary":"What surprises you more? The 4-3 record? Or the fact that three other Clippers (Maggette, Simmons and Wilcox) are doing as much offensive damage as Brand?"},{"week":3,"rank":24,"record":"5-6","summary":"There's only one word to justify why Lakers are so far ahead of their neighbors in these rankings. It's a four-letter word. Yeah, you guessed it: K-O-B-E."},{"week":4,"rank":15,"record":"8-6","summary":"Best team in L.A.? Not quite yet. But it was a better November than anyone could have predicted."},{"week":5,"rank":12,"record":"10-7","summary":"Best team in L.A.? Who cares? The stats say Clippers -- get this -- are the league's best shooting team (.483) and its best passing team (24.5 assists per game)."},{"week":6,"rank":14,"record":"11-8","summary":"Maybe routing Sonics by 30 on opening night gave Clips the confidence to start like this. Two losses to Lakers have been the only downer ... along with Livingston's injury."},{"week":7,"rank":19,"record":"11-12","summary":"Something else that never seems to change in Clipperdom: Clips just can't find a way to win in overtime. They're 1-4 in OT this season and 4-14 since the '01-02 season."},{"week":8,"rank":21,"record":"12-13","summary":"You're not alone if you're starting to think that maybe, just maybe, Clips do owe their early success to that cushy home sked in November. They're a mere 3-7 this month."},{"week":9,"rank":21,"record":"14-15","summary":"Beating Philly took the teetering Clips to 8-3 against the East. Of course, with only 19 games left against Eastern opposition, it's a stretch to suggest they've steadied much."},{"week":10,"rank":16,"record":"16-16","summary":"Surprising as their start was, Clips' stubborness might be the bigger surprise. They didn't fold when things started going bad, as some of you nasty cynics undoubtedly expected."},{"week":11,"rank":16,"record":"18-18","summary":"Lookie here: Clips, all of a sudden, have won three of their past four overtime games -- including Friday's stunner over Shaq's Heat -- after starting 0-3 in OT games this season."},{"week":12,"rank":21,"record":"18-22","summary":"Two wins away from topping the best 37-game start in their California history (19-18 in 1992-93), Clips proceeded to sink from 18-17 to their usual lottery pace with five straight Ls."},{"week":13,"rank":17,"record":"21-23","summary":"It's doubtful Clips can rally back into the West's top eight, but credit them for hanging in without fielding their projected starting five even once (Brand, Maggette, Kaman, Kittles, Jaric)."},{"week":14,"rank":14,"record":"23-24","summary":"San Antonio's seven-game, rodeo-induced road trip is getting all the attention, but don't ignore how Clips are in the midst of a stretch featurning nine in a row on the road."},{"week":15,"rank":22,"record":"23-28","summary":"As we suspected, Clips' forever road trip is proving more merciless than San Antonio's. Clips are 1-5 on their nine-game jaunt and don't play at home again until Feb. 24."},{"week":16,"rank":22,"record":"23-30","summary":"Season of heartbreak continues. Livingston is hurt again and Clips had lost six in a row by a whopping total of 20 points before last Wednesday's blowout loss at Miami."},{"week":17,"rank":22,"record":"25-31","summary":"How ready were Clips to come home? Before this week, their last game at Staples was so long ago that the Super Bowl hadn't been played yet and Jose Canseco's book wasn't out yet."},{"week":18,"rank":22,"record":"26-33","summary":"Clips boast the West's seventh-best home record. But Hornets are the only West club with fewer road wins than L.A.'s six."},{"week":19,"rank":20,"record":"28-35","summary":"If they can manage a 13-6 finish -- a tad optimistic, true -- Clips can halt a league-worst run of 11 straight losing seasons."},{"week":20,"rank":21,"record":"29-37","summary":"Clippers really could have been a contender for No. 8, but they can't win the close ones for the umpteenth straight season. Twelve of L.A.'s last 16 losses are by five points or less."},{"week":21,"rank":19,"record":"32-38","summary":"A letter writer to the LA Times says Kobe didn't choose Lakers over Clips; he turned Lakers into Clips. The standings back  up the claim: Clips are only a half-game behind their neighbors."},{"week":22,"rank":21,"record":"33-41","summary":"Only four times in franchise history -- twice in Buffalo and twice in L.A. -- have Braves/Clips finished with a better record than Lakers. The last time it happened: 1992-93."},{"week":23,"rank":21,"record":"34-43","summary":"A league-leading 12th straight losing season is unavoidable now. But finishing No. 1 in the Staples Center standings will almost certainly work as consolation for these guys."},{"week":24,"rank":18,"record":"36-44","summary":"The magic number to clinch a better record than their Staples Center co-tenants is one. And if not for a season-long injury epidemic, it probably wouldn't have been close."}],"nop":[{"week":1,"rank":24,"record":"0-3","summary":"Coach Scott wasn't kidding when he said he doesn't have time to follow his old team and the J-Kidd saga. The West hasn't been very welcoming, has it?"},{"week":2,"rank":29,"record":"0-6","summary":"Warm welcome to the West continues (not): Baron's back gives out, not for the first time, and five of the next seven games are roadies."},{"week":3,"rank":29,"record":"0-8","summary":"This is just a hunch, but we don't see Hornets turning their own 0-7 start into a 42-40 Cinderella story like Miami did last season. Do you?"},{"week":4,"rank":29,"record":"1-11","summary":"We've identified the problem: Hornets have just one game left in Utah this season. Losing Magliore obviously doubles the pain, although that should hush the Vince trade talk for a bit."},{"week":5,"rank":30,"record":"1-14","summary":"The bad start is a bit more understandable when you remember Hornets are down three All-Stars (Baron, Mash and Magliore). But shouldn't they have won a home game by now? By accident?"},{"week":6,"rank":30,"record":"1-18","summary":"Just checking, but wasn't Charlotte supposed to be the worst team of all time? Hornets' losing streak is 10 now after an eight-gamer to start, and they're 0-4 in those gold unis."},{"week":7,"rank":30,"record":"2-21","summary":"The good news: Hornets finally won a home game. The better news: Wednesday's victory over Golden State means Hornets can't tie Cleveland's 1-27 start from 1970-71."},{"week":8,"rank":30,"record":"2-24","summary":"There was a fear on Bourbon Street that Baron might sit out for months, with the season already gone. It's a bit too late to be a savior, but at least he's back faster than expected."},{"week":9,"rank":30,"record":"2-26","summary":"Can you blame poor Jim Jax? Not only is a trade to Hornets unsettling, but they would be the 11th team he's played for -- one short of tying the Chucky Brown-Tony Massenburg record."},{"week":10,"rank":30,"record":"3-29","summary":"Ouch. Hate to do this to our man Byron Scott, but it must be pointed out that -- even after that stirring OT win over Sacto -- Hornets are still on an 8-74 pace. Hurry back, Magliore."},{"week":11,"rank":29,"record":"5-31","summary":"Baron's latest setback will sound new alarm bells, but Hornets' big week means they're suddenly on an 11-71 pace. At this point, you suspect they'll take that."},{"week":12,"rank":29,"record":"7-33","summary":"Hornets franchise hasn't seen a losing season since 1991-92. They're just nine losses away now, but they'd be even closer if not also in the midst of this 5-4 stretch."},{"week":13,"rank":28,"record":"8-35","summary":"Considering the 2-26 record they lugged into January, Dan Dickau's Hornets can handle whatever happens Monday against Memphis, sporting a 6-9 record this month already."},{"week":14,"rank":30,"record":"8-39","summary":"They've slipped below Bobcats again, but Lord Byron refuses to betray any regret about not waiting for a Laker interview. ''I'm extremely happy where I am,'' he insists."},{"week":15,"rank":28,"record":"10-41","summary":"Lord Byron can relax (a little). Chances are you missed it, but a 2-2 week got New Orleans to safety: 10 wins."},{"week":16,"rank":28,"record":"11-42","summary":"Asked if he's considering a Baron deal this week, GM Bristow says: 'We're not.' Baron probably has to prove his health first, so Hornets can only wait (for that and Magliore's return)."},{"week":17,"rank":28,"record":"11-44","summary":"Having clinched the club's first losing season since 1991-92, and trading Baron, Hornets need a lift. Realistically, though, what goal can they achieve besides finishing ahead of rival Charlotte?"},{"week":18,"rank":28,"record":"13-46","summary":"Miami's 13-0 record against fellow Southeast foes gets all the attention, but the inverse can be found in New Orleans, where Hornets are a perfectly blemished 0-10 vs. Southwest tenants."},{"week":19,"rank":28,"record":"14-47","summary":"It isn't much, but it's something: Hornets are 3-2 in March, which could easily be 4-1. Which means they might actually be pulling away from Charlotte and Atlanta."},{"week":20,"rank":26,"record":"15-50","summary":"Only four more chances remain to spruce up that 0-12 record against Southwest Division neighbors. One game each against Dallas and Memphis, and two more against Houston."},{"week":21,"rank":27,"record":"16-53","summary":"They did it! They did it! With only two chances remaining to finally beat a divisional foe, Hornets stun Memphis to improve to 1-13 against their fellow Southwest tenants."},{"week":22,"rank":24,"record":"17-55","summary":"How unikely was that win in Houston? Yao was out, true, but Hornets became the first team since Sonics in '76 to get 20 points or less from their starters (15 in this case) and still win."},{"week":23,"rank":28,"record":"18-58","summary":"Shinn can certainly answer critics by pointing out that this was Hornets' first losing season since '91-92. But they need to win at least one more game to avoid the worst season in club history."},{"week":24,"rank":29,"record":"18-62","summary":"It's all good. Owner George Shinn, in a recent letter to season-ticket holders, announced that ''I am committed to building a team that will be successful in New Orleans.'' No worries."}],"bkn":[{"week":1,"rank":25,"record":"1-2","summary":"In normal circumstances, Zo's comeback would be heartwarming. Problem is, of course, that Nets are a long, long way from the norm of the past three seasons."},{"week":2,"rank":25,"record":"2-4","summary":"Some encouraging news, at last: J-Kidd says his knee is holding up well and that a December return is the goal. Just don't bet on him staying in Jersey long once he does return."},{"week":3,"rank":26,"record":"2-7","summary":"You knew they'd struggle sans J-Kidd. What you didn't know is they'd be the first team in the shot-clock era to score fewer than 70 points three times in the season's first nine games."},{"week":4,"rank":27,"record":"2-11","summary":"You have to hope Zo continues to speak his mind, no matter what threats management issues, because there's no other reason to pay attention to Jersey . . . until J-Kidd returns."},{"week":5,"rank":20,"record":"4-12","summary":"How glad is Coach Frank to have his point guard back? Without J-Kidd, Nets have exactly one guy (Jefferson at 20.8 ppg) averaging more than 12 points per game."},{"week":6,"rank":19,"record":"7-13","summary":"It won't be easy, true, to find a taker for Kidd's huge contract. But you're going to keep hearing about a possible deal if Nets cave during this tough stretch (13 of 18 on the road)."},{"week":7,"rank":23,"record":"7-16","summary":"Nets can certainly use some vintage Vinsanity, or anything close. Jersey is only 3-4 since Kidd returned and carries an offense (85.7 ppg) better than only Byron Scott's in N'awlins."},{"week":8,"rank":19,"record":"9-16","summary":"The sense here remains that Kidd gets traded . . . provided someone out there is willing to take on his contract. Denver, for example, is more inclined to use Nene as Redd bait."},{"week":9,"rank":20,"record":"11-18","summary":"Because we like to focus on the positive (but really because we still love the Buffalo Braves so much): Vince's 23-point debut tied ex-Brave Bird Averitt for the No. 2 bow in Nets history."},{"week":10,"rank":25,"record":"12-21","summary":"Not sure why this Vince interview on TNT has caused such an uproar. No real mystery here -- if you're trying to get traded, sadly, withholding some effort can speed things up sometimes."},{"week":11,"rank":25,"record":"12-24","summary":"Can't understand why they're trying so hard to trade for Jim Jax or Uncle Cliffy. Hate to run off all their fans, but Nets -- with RJ suddenly gone -- are better off sandbagging for the lottery."},{"week":12,"rank":22,"record":"15-25","summary":"Hanging in there at 3-4 without RJ, so who knows? Maybe Nets can still come back and win this sorry division, even though we still say Kidd's knee is better saved for future endeavors."},{"week":13,"rank":20,"record":"18-26","summary":"All of our friends who are Nets fans (granted, that's just Sanford and O-lee) swear NJ is going to come back and win the Atlantic. The way Vince is starting to play, maybe they're right."},{"week":14,"rank":18,"record":"20-27","summary":"The only team in the Atlantic that hasn't led the division yet is the one that scares everyone right now, with Vince -- dare we say it -- looking worthy of his All-Star spot. Ditto for J-Kidd."},{"week":15,"rank":14,"record":"22-29","summary":"As if Vince's renaissance and a 10-5 uptick doesn't have everyone else in the Atlantic worried, Jefferson is vowing to come back for the playoffs like Terrell Owens did."},{"week":16,"rank":16,"record":"23-30","summary":"Kidd has three triple-doubles in his past six games entering Tuesday's Vince return to Toronto. So, no, Nets are obviously in no rush to move him."},{"week":17,"rank":18,"record":"25-32","summary":"Just like that, after what Philly and Boston did, you aren't hearing many folks claiming Nets can still win the Atlantic."},{"week":18,"rank":20,"record":"26-34","summary":"For all the hoopla since the trade, the reality is this: Nets have slipped to 17-18 in the Vinsanity era."},{"week":19,"rank":21,"record":"28-36","summary":"It hasn't been a pretty month in Jersey. You don't hear much talk about the playoffs now after four heavy losses (by an average of 20.3 ppg) and a near-loss at New Orleans."},{"week":20,"rank":15,"record":"31-36","summary":"Just when it appeared you could exclude Jersey from playoff consideration, this is the only Eastern Conference resident outside the top three on any kind of roll."},{"week":21,"rank":18,"record":"32-38","summary":"Whether or not Nets claim that No. 8 spot, they have to be somewhat encouraged by their 19-17 record since losing Jefferson. Jersey easily could have folded instead."},{"week":22,"rank":19,"record":"35-39","summary":"The more we think about it, the harder it is to see how snaring the East's final playoff berth will make a huge difference to Kidd when it comes to his wanting to stay or go."},{"week":23,"rank":15,"record":"38-39","summary":"Nets haven't visited the .500 Club since Nov. 9. But they're closing in on it now and can secure a franchise-record-tying fourth straight winning season with a 4-1 finish."},{"week":24,"rank":13,"record":"40-40","summary":"The way Nets are rolling, it looks as though they'll snare the eighth spot. But if they don't, Nets can point to a league-leading 13 losses in which they led by at least 10 points."}],"nyk":[{"week":1,"rank":26,"record":"0-2","summary":"Can't say it better than the NY Times, which writes that 'their defense is nonexistent, their best shooter is in street clothes and their hole at center has rarely looked larger.'"},{"week":2,"rank":24,"record":"2-3","summary":"It's a good thing Lenny beat Philly and Clips, because wins figure to be scarce this week with injury-hit Knicks in Texas to make all three stops on the dreaded triangle."},{"week":3,"rank":18,"record":"4-5","summary":"Though they've been a .500 team this season for less than 24 hours, give Knicks some credit. They handled the dreaded Texas Triangle better than anyone expected."},{"week":4,"rank":17,"record":"6-6","summary":"Isiah has said he wants to be .500, at worst, after 20 games. Us? We want to see how Lenny handles Allan Houston's return with Jamal Crawford surging."},{"week":5,"rank":19,"record":"8-8","summary":"Just when you think they've turned a corner, Knicks lose to Orlando and Charlotte to remind us how much trouble they've had in the new millennium just playing .500 ball."},{"week":6,"rank":18,"record":"10-10","summary":"As Isiah requested, Lenny made it through the first 20 games at .500. If they can keep it up amid the usual trade-talk pressures, the Atlantic is there to be won."},{"week":7,"rank":14,"record":"13-11","summary":"Isiah's one-year anniversary with Knicks is Wednesday -- with only three players left from the team he inherited, and two (Houston and K. Thomas) available for the next trade."},{"week":8,"rank":17,"record":"14-13","summary":"Amid Isiah one-year anniversary celebrations, Knicks fall behind by 39 (AT THE HALF!) at home to Dallas, then blow one in Boston. An Isiah response must be forthcoming."},{"week":9,"rank":15,"record":"16-14","summary":"This is the only Atlantic Division representative to make it to 2005 with a better-than-.500 record. One big reason: Knicks are actually 5-1 at home against West opposition."},{"week":10,"rank":17,"record":"17-17","summary":"The committee's MSG spies offered a clear warning: Don't be surprised if Wilkens goes this week. If Isiah had a clear-cut interim option, it probably would have happened already."},{"week":11,"rank":19,"record":"17-19","summary":"Injuries have been a factor, true, but Knicks should be a fair bit better than 1-6 in 2005. Shouldn't they?"},{"week":12,"rank":24,"record":"17-23","summary":"New Yorkers can dream, but we can't see the Zenmeister taking on a team with no size, a bloated payroll, an aversion to D and two shoot-first franchise guards (Marbury and Crawford)."},{"week":13,"rank":25,"record":"18-25","summary":"It might be their worst January ever at 2-12 -- Knicks went 3-14 in January 1963 -- but the past week was their best week all season. Phil and Larry showed interest in working with Isiah."},{"week":14,"rank":26,"record":"18-29","summary":"For those wondering why Steph won't make even the East's All-Star snubbed list, don't forget New York is, uh, 2-16 in 2005."},{"week":15,"rank":23,"record":"20-31","summary":"Have to share a recent gem from committee fave Mark Heisler of the L.A. Times: ''There's no truth to the rumor Stern is prepared to go to 30 divisions so the Knicks can finish first.''"},{"week":16,"rank":23,"record":"21-32","summary":"It hasn't been pretty, has it? What else can you say with Knicks at 4-10 in the Herb Williams Era?"},{"week":17,"rank":25,"record":"23-33","summary":"It's a bit bizarre to see Knicks swinging a deal with Spurs. The contracts of A. Houston, T. Thomas and Penny combined roughly equal San Antonio's total payroll."},{"week":18,"rank":23,"record":"25-34","summary":"Bold prediction: This will not be the spring that Steph wins his first playoff series, in spite of Knicks' recent 6-3 uptick."},{"week":19,"rank":22,"record":"26-35","summary":"You hate to be negative after Knicks' longest home winning streak (seven) since the spring of 2001. But the fact remains that they're 0-13 against teams at the .600 level or better."},{"week":20,"rank":25,"record":"27-37","summary":"Bold prediction II: Three losing seasons is about to become four, because Knicks -- with just two road wins in 2005 -- have way too many roadies left (10) to finish 14-4."},{"week":21,"rank":23,"record":"29-39","summary":"We like Herb as much as anyone, but c'mon. Everyone saying he deserves the job full-time forgets that Knicks still lose a lot of close games and haven't exactly made a playoff charge."},{"week":22,"rank":25,"record":"29-43","summary":"More bad news for Steph. Suns' success makes it three straight teams to win at least 50 games in their first full season after Steph leaves (along with Wolves and Nets)."},{"week":23,"rank":23,"record":"30-46","summary":"Did J-Kidd really add any lasting spice to the rivalry by calling Knicks ''a bad team''? Who can argue with him? Nets have won 17 of the past 20 meetings; NY has four straight losing seasons."},{"week":24,"rank":24,"record":"32-48","summary":"On Jan. 1, at 16-13, a playoff berth seemed reasonable. Zeke's Knicks have won only 16 games since, and only that many because they're 3-0 on the road after a 2-20 away stretch."}],"gsw":[{"week":1,"rank":27,"record":"0-3","summary":"Mike Montgomery, whose Stanford team lost only twice last season, could be looking at a 1-7 start. Charlotte is the only inviting stop on an upcoming five-game trip."},{"week":2,"rank":26,"record":"1-6","summary":"Only Hornets' ultimate shame -- falling below Charlotte -- nudged Warriors up one spot. Because they're up high on the list of early disappointments."},{"week":3,"rank":27,"record":"2-8","summary":"At 0-7 against Western opposition, Warriors (and Montgomery) have to know that they're out of the playoff race already. Barring a miracle for the rookie coach."},{"week":4,"rank":28,"record":"3-10","summary":"We've identified the problem: Warriors are undefeated as a franchise when they go to triple-overtime . . . but, including last week, it's only happened three times in their history."},{"week":5,"rank":28,"record":"4-12","summary":"They've got Mully and Richmond in the front office . . . and not a soul on the roster who can shoot anything like either one. And with no shooters, Warriors can't score."},{"week":6,"rank":28,"record":"6-14","summary":"It was only a matter of time, wasn't it? The first rumblings of player discontent with the rookie coach from the college ranks are starting to make the national rounds."},{"week":7,"rank":27,"record":"7-17","summary":"With a chance to improve to 8-8 since their 0-8 start, what happened? Warriors followed up a breakthrough win in Dallas by becoming the first team to lose at New Orleans."},{"week":8,"rank":27,"record":"9-18","summary":"Warriors can't revel in Dampier's Dallas struggles because the center they did re-sign (Foyle) is struggling worse. Hence Uncle Cliffy's emergence as the new C in GS."},{"week":9,"rank":24,"record":"10-19","summary":"The improvement is tangible; Warriors are 8-7 over the past 15 games. But they were so disappointing early that Warrior Nation, if there is such a thing, should expect a slow climb."},{"week":10,"rank":26,"record":"11-23","summary":"Just when it seemed a narrow L to the Washington Warriors Alumni Club might turn around its season, GS lost J-Rich and is skidding since a four-game win streak."},{"week":11,"rank":27,"record":"11-27","summary":"Word on the street is that Warriors are in no hurry to move Uncle Cliffy, no matter what you've read, because they liked how the team was playing before J-Rich went down. No lie."},{"week":12,"rank":27,"record":"12-29","summary":"The season is a lost cause already, but it's not this guy's fault: Murphy has averaged nearly 14 rebounds over the past 15 games. And he's draining his threes, too."},{"week":13,"rank":27,"record":"12-32","summary":"Typical. A thumb injury intrudes on Murphy's bid to be the first player in the top five in rebounding and 3-point shooting percentage since Larry Legend way back in 1985-86."},{"week":14,"rank":28,"record":"13-34","summary":"In yet another wasted season, the only solace is that half of the $200-plus million spent over the summer -- the J-Rich and Murphy half -- is making a game effort to live up to its price tag."},{"week":15,"rank":27,"record":"14-37","summary":"Warriors put some heat on Johnny Davis by beating Orlando, then gave Phoenix a scare, but the fact remains: Golden State is 3-22 since a four-game win streak to close 2004."},{"week":16,"rank":26,"record":"15-38","summary":"Over his final six seasons at Stanford, Montgomery lost 35 games. In the pros, he might not even make it to March of his first season with fewer than 40 losses."},{"week":17,"rank":27,"record":"16-39","summary":"This will be Warriors' 11th straight season out of the playoffs. Not that Baron minds after likening his Hornets stint to ''prison.''"},{"week":18,"rank":27,"record":"18-41","summary":"Baron is clearly still shaking off the rust. Dare we say he's not a 31-percent shooter, as seen so far with Warriors."},{"week":19,"rank":25,"record":"20-43","summary":"Warriors finished a brutal eight-game trip at 4-4. They prefer to focus on that as opposed to Montgomery needing until March to secure his 20th victory. Not a good thing in the pros."},{"week":20,"rank":22,"record":"23-44","summary":"Who saw this coming? With two wins over Sacramento sandwiched around a road upset of Phoenix, Montgomery is suddenly having a better March than Stanford."},{"week":21,"rank":20,"record":"24-45","summary":"Montgomery says Baron is getting too much credit. Huh? GS is 6-4 on the road with Baron ... and 5-21 without him."},{"week":22,"rank":17,"record":"28-45","summary":"Trivia time: Who has the best record in Cali since the All-Star break? Yup: Warriors are 13-7; Lakers are last at 7-16."},{"week":23,"rank":17,"record":"31-46","summary":"Warriors desperately want to believe this late-season run means something for next season ... and that the draft choice affected by all this recent winning wouldn't be that helpful anyway."},{"week":24,"rank":17,"record":"32-48","summary":"They've faded a little, sure, since that record-setting road win streak. But it's been a fun ride since Baron arrived, as Ws over Suns (twice), Kings  (twice), Rockets and Sonics would suggest."}],"chi":[{"week":1,"rank":28,"record":"0-2","summary":"For some reason, Bulls didn't play a game until the season was four days old. Which will lead some wise guys to the inevitable crack about how that still was too soon."},{"week":2,"rank":30,"record":"0-4","summary":"Next seven games are roadies . . . after Bulls blew 24-point home lead to Clips . . .  after Bulls shot 1-for-21 on 3-pointers against Phoenix."},{"week":3,"rank":30,"record":"0-8","summary":"This is just a hunch, but we don't see Bulls following the Miami blueprint and turning their own 0-7 start into a 42-40 Cinderella story like Heat did last season. Do you?"},{"week":4,"rank":30,"record":"1-10","summary":"We've identified the problem: Bulls have no games left in Utah this season . . . and can't keep the circus from coming to Chicago so early, which starts every season with a killer trip."},{"week":5,"rank":27,"record":"2-12","summary":"If you're willing to twist this stat into a cause for optimism, Bulls can claim history is on their side. In 1976-77, Chicago went 0-10 in November and still made the playoffs."},{"week":6,"rank":24,"record":"4-14","summary":"Still haven't won two games in a row, but why quibble? Routing Cleveland and holding off Minny might have made this Chicago's best week in years."},{"week":7,"rank":22,"record":"7-15","summary":"Kudos for the three-game win streak and 6-5 start to December after a 1-10 November. However ... we're still skeptical. Baby Bulls have teased before."},{"week":8,"rank":20,"record":"9-16","summary":"A case can be made that we've been too tough on those Baby Bulls. With only two teams over .500 among the next eight games, they have a real chance to make it a stronger case."},{"week":9,"rank":23,"record":"10-17","summary":"Even after two downer losses to close the calendar year, Bulls posted an 8-7 mark in December. Even the committee can applaud those numbers."},{"week":10,"rank":19,"record":"13-18","summary":"Committee has been shamed into more applause for Bulls. Reason being: Chicago, since its 2-13 start, is  second-best in the East (at 11-5) behind Miami (14-2 in the same span)."},{"week":11,"rank":17,"record":"16-18","summary":"Call them this year's version of last season's Heat. Because it looks like Bulls -- having held 21 straight opponents under 100 points -- really are rebounding from a dreadful start."},{"week":12,"rank":16,"record":"19-19","summary":"The good news: Bulls still lead the league in FG defense at .410. The better news: Chicago hasn't been at .500 later than 2-2 (in '02-03) in any season since MJ retired ... until now."},{"week":13,"rank":14,"record":"22-20","summary":"There's a reason why, in Week 3, we questioned Bulls' ability to rally from an 0-9 start. Reason being: Chicago is the first team ever to open 0-8 (or worse) and then surpass .500."},{"week":14,"rank":13,"record":"22-22","summary":"Can't say it better than gritty, gutty Scotty Skiles, who says: ''We're not an 0-9 team, but we're not an 18-4 team, either.'' Maybe this month's heavy road schedule will clarify things."},{"week":15,"rank":12,"record":"24-23","summary":"Bulls already have two surprise W's in a killer month. But they can't celebrate yet; eight of the next 13 games are roadies."},{"week":16,"rank":8,"record":"26-23","summary":"Who's hotter than Memphis and Dallas? Who's as hot as Houston and Detroit? Bulls' record since Jan. 1 is 17-6, tied with Rockets and Pistons for the league's best in the span."},{"week":17,"rank":8,"record":"29-24","summary":"Now that he has passed James Worthy, Gordon is chasing Jeff Ruland's total of 19 20-point games off the bench in his rookie season of 1981-82. Gordon has 14 as a sub."},{"week":18,"rank":15,"record":"29-27","summary":"Baby Bulls hung tough in February with a solid 7-4 mark. But their March schedule is even tougher (18 games) than last month's and the alarm bells have sounded after an 0-3 start."},{"week":19,"rank":13,"record":"32-28","summary":"Air Gordon is what they're apparently calling Chicago's surprising rookie sixth man. Let's see if they're still winning enough by the end of a crazy March to be passing out nicknames."},{"week":20,"rank":16,"record":"33-31","summary":"After going 7-4 in February, Bulls are 4-7 in March and still have seven more games to play this month. And it hasn't helped matters that they're 0-4 against New Jersey."},{"week":21,"rank":9,"record":"37-31","summary":"Winning five in a row at this point -- three on the road -- is as impressive as anything these Bulls have achieved. So it's almost time, for the first time since '98, to print up playoff tickets."},{"week":22,"rank":8,"record":"41-31","summary":"It looks safer and safer to put the 0-9 No Mores in the same club with Phoenix when it comes to making the playoffs after a dreadful start. Suns, remember, opened 0-13 in '96-97."},{"week":23,"rank":7,"record":"44-32","summary":"We can understand Jerry Reinsdorf's concerns about spending big on Curry and Chandler. But someone is going to have to explain why Skiles doesn't have a long-term extension yet."},{"week":24,"rank":9,"record":"46-34","summary":"Don't write Baby Bulls off in the first round, even without Curry and Deng. They're 14-2 since a worrisome four-game skid."}],"cha":[{"week":1,"rank":29,"record":"1-1","summary":"Became the 11th of 18 expansion teams in NBA history to lose their opening game. Of course, Bobcats forgot all about that after the thrills of Game 2."},{"week":2,"rank":28,"record":"1-4","summary":"Uh-oh. Bobcats' hopes of winning something -- Okafor for Rookie of the Year -- have already been compromised with the way Dwight Howard is flexing in Orlando."},{"week":3,"rank":27,"record":"1-8","summary":"Getting fans in the building has been tougher than expected, but it looks as though Bobcats are mastering the art of the excruciating loss. They've got three already."},{"week":4,"rank":25,"record":"3-9","summary":"What a night for Brevin Knight on Tuesday. With 19 assists, he had three more than the whole Detroit team."},{"week":5,"rank":24,"record":"4-10","summary":"How sweet must these numbers be: With a payroll that comes in about $5 million under Shaq's $27.7 million salary, Bobcats are on a 23-59 pace. Stunning."},{"week":6,"rank":29,"record":"4-14","summary":"Bobcats still have a healthy lead on New Orleans and still have a .500 record at home (4-4). Things could be much worse."},{"week":7,"rank":25,"record":"6-14","summary":"It just gets better and better. Bobcats have won five straight at home to set a 25-win pace, and Okafor has posted 12 -- count 'em, 12 -- consecutive double-doubles."},{"week":8,"rank":24,"record":"7-16","summary":"The team that wasn't supposed to win 10 games all season had seven wins at Christmas. Which is probably the biggest reason why Okafor leads most ROY ballots."},{"week":9,"rank":28,"record":"7-20","summary":"The numbers are nice for Okafor and even Brevin Knight, but here's a better compliment: Bobs haven't won a game for two weeks . . . and that surprised us when we counted it up."},{"week":10,"rank":27,"record":"8-22","summary":"Bobcats can deal with their recent 1-7 slide because the one win in there was so sweet, with the expansionites scoring 24 of the game's final 28 points to slay Wolves."},{"week":11,"rank":28,"record":"8-25","summary":"Wins have dried up for Bobcats, but Okafor should be an All-Star reserve in the East, rookie or not. We'll argue that Emeka and Jamison are the East's most deserving forwards."},{"week":12,"rank":28,"record":"8-29","summary":"In the midst of their longest losing streak of the season, Bobcats quickly fall from a 23-59 pace to an 18-64 pace. Worse yet, Hornets and Hawks are gaining on them in the Rankings."},{"week":13,"rank":29,"record":"9-32","summary":"A home win over Toronto is nothing special, but Bobcats needed it to keep from sliding to the bottom of the rankings for the first time since the preseason. So for them it was special."},{"week":14,"rank":27,"record":"10-34","summary":"As long as it's not another back injury. Bobcats can live with Emeka's ankle trouble. Especially since they quietly scored victory No. 10 without him, long before anyone expected."},{"week":15,"rank":30,"record":"10-38","summary":"What a difference two months (and no Okafor) makes. On Dec. 5, Bobcats could claim a 5-14 record and thus were having a better season than Chicago (5-15 at the time)."},{"week":16,"rank":29,"record":"11-39","summary":"Bobcats needed the All-Star break to get rest for Emeka and Brevin, and now they need a break after losing to those two recent buzzer-beaters against Portland and New York."},{"week":17,"rank":29,"record":"11-42","summary":"A healthy ankle isn't enough. Okafor really has to pick up his road production to hold off Gordon for ROY honors, after averaging 6.0 ppg over a recent span of six roadies."},{"week":18,"rank":29,"record":"12-45","summary":"If current form holds, Bobcats will finish with 17 victories. Of course, Okafor winning Rookie of the Year is what they're really chasing in the final month-plus."},{"week":19,"rank":30,"record":"12-48","summary":"Since that crucial 10th victory, Bobcats are 2-16. The wins were good (Nuggets, Kings) but you have to wonder how low they can go after that fall-from-ahead, Kobe-inflicted heartbreak."},{"week":20,"rank":30,"record":"12-52","summary":"Yes, you guessed right: After a long lean spell, Bobcats have already circled their two Atlanta games next month."},{"week":21,"rank":25,"record":"15-53","summary":"Our math has never been as good as our father's -- you're the man, Reuvs -- but something tells us that the committee's 13-69 prediction for the expansionites is in trouble."},{"week":22,"rank":27,"record":"15-57","summary":"We're pulling for a surging Brevin Knight to get that assist average into double digits. The NBA hasn't had two 10-assist men since Stock and our man Mark Jackson in '96-97."},{"week":23,"rank":29,"record":"15-61","summary":"Oh, well. Even after averaging 11 apg over his past 11 games, Brevin Knight would need to average 19.5 dimes in Charlotte's final six games to get his average into double digits."},{"week":24,"rank":28,"record":"17-63","summary":"In the end, Bobs couldn't secure the first three-game win streak in club history. But seeing Bobs with 17 wins still shocks us almost as much as seeing Utah with only 25."}],"atl":[{"week":1,"rank":30,"record":"0-3","summary":"Hawks were supposed to be able to say, 'Thank God for Charlotte.' Unfortunately, they can't even say that because Bobcats look sharper."},{"week":2,"rank":27,"record":"1-5","summary":"Thanks to realignment, Hawks have only one game left against New Orleans. So, no, Hawks aren't celebrating their victory (or their rankings rise) too much."},{"week":3,"rank":25,"record":"2-7","summary":"Put them at the top of the scrap-heap section for that comeback win over Houston . . . and signs that they're looking slightly more competitive. Slightly."},{"week":4,"rank":26,"record":"2-11","summary":"It's getting close to official. You'd have to say gutty Bobcats are the better team."},{"week":5,"rank":29,"record":"2-14","summary":"In the quest to come up with something -- anything -- positive, all we can tell you is Hawks have the league's best 40-year-old. In fact, at age 42, Kevin Willis is the only 40-year-old."},{"week":6,"rank":26,"record":"4-16","summary":"Hawks have yet to score 100 points in regulation this season. Not that said failure stopped their new coach from picking up a ring and then humbling the defending champs."},{"week":7,"rank":29,"record":"4-20","summary":"It's not getting any better, is it? Since thoroughly embarrassing Detroit, Hawks have dropped five in a row . . . by a combined 77 points. Wish we were kidding."},{"week":8,"rank":28,"record":"5-20","summary":"He's not going to fill up Philips Arena, since no one can do that, but the rookie Smith is worth watching. Anyone who can block five Nowitzki shots in one game gets me curious."},{"week":9,"rank":29,"record":"5-24","summary":"When we said no one can fill Philips Arena, of course we meant no one on the Atlanta roster. Just wanted to clarify, since LeBron, for example, has proven he can do it."},{"week":10,"rank":29,"record":"5-26","summary":"It probably won't get him to the All-Star Game, but this is good company for 'Toine -- KG and R. Jefferson are the only other guys leading their teams in points, rebounds and assists."},{"week":11,"rank":30,"record":"7-27","summary":"It brings us no joy to bring this up, but Hawks are the only team in the league that hasn't won two straight games yet. And FYI: Atlanta needed until February to do so last season."},{"week":12,"rank":30,"record":"8-30","summary":"We're using this for the second week in a row just so Atlanta can repeat something: Hawks are the only team in the league that hasn't won two games in a row yet."},{"week":13,"rank":30,"record":"8-34","summary":"This won't help ticket sales, either: Hawks are two defeats away from setting a new club record for losses at the All-Star break ... with nine games to go before the break."},{"week":14,"rank":29,"record":"9-37","summary":"With 12 double-doubles in 19 games, 'Toine is trying to get noticed for All-Star consideration. Atlanta simply loses too much."},{"week":15,"rank":29,"record":"10-39","summary":"If you're wondering why 'Toine really hasn't been mentioned anywhere as an All-Star snubee, you must have missed that Hawks' road losing streak has reached 14. And counting."},{"week":16,"rank":30,"record":"10-41","summary":"Philips Arena should be half-full every night just because Josh Smith is there. Shouldn't it?"},{"week":17,"rank":30,"record":"10-45","summary":"After an 0-4 return to reality, All-Star Weekend seems as far removed from the present as that Nique jersey Josh Smith wore in the dunk contest. 'Toine won't miss the place."},{"week":18,"rank":30,"record":"10-48","summary":"How many games ago do you think Coach Woodson started thinking that perhaps he should have just stayed in Detroit and waited out Larry's Brown departure?"},{"week":19,"rank":29,"record":"11-51","summary":"What a week. Hawks finally won a road game after 23 consecutive away defeats ... and Ty Lue topped the 25-point plateau in consecutive games for the first time in his career."},{"week":20,"rank":29,"record":"11-54","summary":"Well, it's back to reality after the breakthrough road triumph in Toronto. Hawks just completed an 0-4 homestand, surrendering no fewer than 106 points in any of the losses."},{"week":21,"rank":30,"record":"11-58","summary":"Hawks are on the verge of joining Clips of '86-87 (12-70) and 1947-48's Providence Steamrollers (6-42) as the only teams in history to go a whole season without winning two in a row."},{"week":22,"rank":30,"record":"11-62","summary":"Obinna Ekezie is Woodson's center and Royal Ivey is his point guard. Which is another way of saying that, yes, the rookie coach deserves the No. 1 overall pick for his suffering."},{"week":23,"rank":30,"record":"12-64","summary":"Driving the stake into Minnesota's season is only half of what Atlanta accomplished Saturday night. The big news is Hawks have finally surpassed Falcons' regular-season win total of 11."},{"week":24,"rank":30,"record":"13-67","summary":"At least they avoided 70 losses. Not by much, but Hawks -- after losing back-to-back games to Charlotte to make sure they have the most lottery pingpong balls -- achieved that much."}]},"playoffs":{"phi":"first-round","det":"finals","ind":"semis","bos":"first-round","bkn":"first-round","mia":"conf-finals","was":"semis","chi":"first-round","hou":"first-round","dal":"semis","mem":"first-round","phx":"conf-finals","den":"first-round","sas":"champion","sac":"first-round","okc":"semis"}}
